ess Park Addition, 5034 Frankford\nAvenue, Tract A, Luskey Addition, 5052 Frankford Avenue, Lot 6-A, Frankford Business Park\nAddition, 5602 Frankford Avenue, 0.73 acres of unplatted land out of Block AK, Section 36, 5610\nFrankford Avenue, Lot 1, Frankford Business Park Addition, 5820 Spur 327, 4.01 acres of unplatted\nland out of Block AK, Section 36, 5802 Spur 327, Tracts A and B, Womble Addition, 5702 – 5828\nGenoa Avenue, Lots 1-11, Heron Development Addition, 5911 57th Street, 6.88 acres of unplatted land\nout of Block AK, Section 36, 6000 Spur 327, Tracts A and B, Bob Mills Furniture Company Addition,\n5423, 5425, and 5435 Frankford Avenue, Tracts 1-A, 1-B, and 1-C, C C Knott Addition, 5613\nFrankford Avenue, Tract A, Carizma Motors Addition, 5617, 5621, and 5701 Frankford Avenue, Lots\n8, 2-A, 2-B, 27, and 28, Westac Addition, 5310 Englewood Avenue, Lot 25, Westac Addition, 5320\nEnglewood Avenue, 1.39 acres of unplatted land out of Block E-2, Section 28, 5614 and 5618\nEnglewood Avenue, Lots 26-A and 26-B, Westac Addition, 5610, 5702, and 5712 58th Street, Lots 7,\n10, 11-A, 17, and 23, Westac Addition, 5310, 5320, 5612, and 5620, West Loop 289, Lots 16, 20, 22,\nand 24, Westac Addition, 5801, 5805, and 5807 Frankford Avenue, Lots 1-A-1, 3-A, and 4-A-1,\nWestac Addition, 5702, 5706, 5708 and 5720 Spur 327, Lot\ns 2-A, 3, 4, and 6, Village Center Addition,\n5710 and 5716 Spur 327, Lots 6-A-1 and 6-A-2, Westac Addition, 5725 and 5727 58th "}, {"title": "2026-06-22 - Parks and Recreation Advisory Board - 12:00 PM (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06222026-100", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "William Pasewark, Chair Ella O’Neal, Vice Chair Shelby Cotton Kim Davis Michael Henson Michael King Veronica Lopez Keith C. Thompson Timothy Weaver Parks and Recreation Advisory Board Agenda June 22, 2026 12:00 P.M. Citizens Tower 2nd Floor 201B, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas Parks and Recreation Advisory Board meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If y", "text": "William Pasewark, Chair \nElla O’Neal, Vice Chair \nShelby Cotton \nKim Davis \nMichael Henson \nMichael King \nVeronica Lopez \nKeith C. Thompson \nTimothy Weaver \n\nParks and Recreation Advisory Board \nAgenda \nJune 22, 2026 \n12:00 P.M. \n \nCitizens Tower 2nd Floor 201B, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, \nTexas \n\nParks and Recreation Advisory Board meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special \nassistance, please contact the City of Lubbock at 775-2673 or write to P.O. Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas, 79457, at least 48 \nhours in advance of the meeting. \n\n1. Call to Order \n \n2. Citizen Comments – Any citizen wishing to appear before a regular meeting of the Park Advisory Board, regarding any \nmatter posted on the Park Board Agenda below, shall complete the sign-up form provided at the meeting, no later than \n12:00 p.m. Any citizen wishing to comment on any matter posted on the Park Advisory Agenda below that will not attend \nin person may submit a citizen comment by email at SCantu@mylubbock.us, no later than 12:00 p.m. on the date of the \nmeeting. Submitted comments must include name and address. Each comment will be read aloud for a period not to exceed \nthree minutes. Citizen Comments is an opportunity for citizens to make comments and express a position on agenda items. \nAny comment received that is in the nature of asking a question will be referred to an appropriate member of the City staff \nfor a response and will not be read aloud at the meeting. \n \n3. Approval of Minutes \n \n3.1 \nJanuary 12, 2026 \n\n4. Work Session \n \n4.1 \nIntroduction of new park board members \n4.2 \n2026 Capital Improvement Project updates - Colby VanGundy - Director of Parks and Recreation \n \n5. Action Item \n \n 5.1 Adopt-A-Park - Consider various organizations, as approved by the Lubbock Park Board, to adopt community parks \n as part of the new Adopt-A-Park program - Colby VanGundy - Director of Parks and Recreation \n6. Adjourn \n \n Date of next scheduled meeting: July 27, 2026 \nThe above referenced NOTICE OF MEETING was posted on the bulletin board outside the east entrance of \nCitizens Tower, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas, on the _____________ day of __________________, 2026 at \n_____________ AM/PM. \n \nBy: ____________________________________________"}, {"title": "2026-06-17 - Upland Crossing Public Improvement District Advisory Board Regular Meeting - 9:00 AM (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06172026-97", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "The above referenced NOTICE OF MEETING was posted outside the South entrance of Citizens Tower, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas, on the _____ day of ____________, 2026 at________A.M./P.M. ___________________________________ Austin Lear, Chair Trey Benton, Vice Chair Jordan Rodgers Jennifer Tollett Upland Crossing Public Improvement District Advisory Board Regular Meeting Agenda June 17", "text": "The above referenced NOTICE OF MEETING was posted outside the South entrance of Citizens Tower, 1314 \nAvenue K, Lubbock, Texas, on the _____ day of ____________, 2026 at________A.M./P.M. \n\n ___________________________________ \n\nAustin Lear, Chair \nTrey Benton, Vice Chair \nJordan Rodgers \nJennifer Tollett \n\nUpland Crossing Public Improvement District \nAdvisory Board Regular Meeting Agenda \n June 17, 2026 | 9:00 A.M. \nMicrosoft Teams Link: \nhttps://teams.microsoft.com/meet/24753043958185?p=DtzuOcUWIOhZqs2D6N \nMeeting ID: 251 148 071 359 892 Passcode: AE7AY2bZ \n \nMolly Ballesteros, \nSpecial Districts Manager \nDanielle Williams, \nBusiness Development \nDirector \n\nUpland Crossing Public Improvement District meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special \nassistance, please contact the Business Development Department at 806.775.3083, e-mail businessdevelopment@mylubbock.us, or \nwrite to Post Office Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas 79457 at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting. \n \n1. \nCall to order \n \n2. \nCitizen Comments - Any citizen wishing to address the Upland Crossing Public Improvement \nDistrict \nAdvisory \nBoard, \nmay \nsubmit \na \ncitizen \ncomment \nby \nemail \nat \nbusinessdevelopment@mylubbock.us no later than 5 p.m. on the date before the meeting. \nSubmitted comments must include name and address. Citizen Comments is an opportunity for \ncitizens to make comments and express a position on agenda items. Each comment will be read \naloud for a period of time not to exceed three minutes pursuant to City Council rules. Any comment \nreceived that is in the nature of asking a question will be referred to an appropriate member of the \nCity staff for a response. \n \n3. \nFinancial Report \n \n4. \nRegular Session \n \n4.1 \nApproval of Minutes \nOctober 21, 2025 \nJanuary 6, 2026 \nFebruary 13, 2026 \nMarch 11, 2026 \n \n4.2 \nDiscuss and take appropriate action on the Fiscal Year 2026-27 Service and \nAssessment Plan \n \n5. \nWork Session \n \n5.1 \nPlaya Lake Park Stormwater Drainage Remediation Project Update \n \n5.2 \n2026 Annual Property Owner Meeting Discussion \n \n6. \nSchedule Next Meeting – The next proposed meeting day is August 4, 2026, at 11:30 a.m."}, {"title": "2026-06-17 - Permit & License Appeal Board - 11:30 AM (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06172026-98", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "1. Call to order 2. Public Comment - Any citizen wishing to appear before a regular meeting of the Permit & License Appeal Board regarding any matter posted on the Permit & License Appeal Board Agenda may speak. 3. Minutes 3.1 May 20, 2026 Permit & License Appeal Board Meeting 4. Regular Session 4.1 Junked Vehicle Determinations - May be enacted by one motion without separa", "text": "1. \nCall to order \n \n2. \nPublic Comment - Any citizen wishing to appear before a regular meeting of the Permit \n& License Appeal Board regarding any matter posted on the Permit & License Appeal \nBoard Agenda may speak. \n \n3. \nMinutes \n \n3.1 \nMay 20, 2026 Permit & License Appeal Board Meeting \n \n4. \nRegular Session \n \n4.1 \nJunked Vehicle Determinations - May be enacted by one motion without \nseparate discussion. If the Permit & License Appeal Board desires to discuss an \nitem, the item is removed and considered separately. \n \n4.1.1 CASE NO: JV-2026-011514 of Inspector Randy Merrick regarding one \n(1) vehicle at 121 79th St. \n \n4.1.2 CASE NO: JV-2026-011666 of Inspector Tyler Brewer regarding one (1) \nvehicle at 2601 Fir Ave. \n \n4.1.3 CASE NO: JV-2026-011873 of Inspector Courtney Brackeen regarding \none (1) vehicle at 8703 Dover Ave. \n \nGarrott Nalle, Chair \nJillian Nava, Vice Chair \nCecile Garcia \nBrooks Jones \nThomas Nichols \nDavid Saunders \nDonald Stubbs \n \nPermit & License Appeal Board \nAgenda \nJune 17, 2026 \n11:30 A.M. \nCourtney Paz, City Secretary \nJimmy Maynard, Deputy City \nSecretary \nRyan Brooke, Assistant City \nAttorney \n \nCitizens Tower \nCity Council Chambers, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas \n\nPermit & License Appeal Board meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special \nassistance, please contact the Office of the City Secretary at 806.775.2061, e-mail ocs@mylubbock.us, or write to \nPost Office Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas 79457 at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting. \n \nExecutive Session Disclosure Statement: The Permit & License Appeal Board reserves the right to recess into \nexecutive session at any time during the course of the meeting to discuss any item listed on this agenda as authorized \nby Chapter 551 of the Texas Government Code, including but not necessarily limited to §551.071 (Consultation with \nAttorney), §551.072 (Deliberations regarding Real Property), §551.073 (Deliberations regarding Gifts and \nDonations), §551.074 (Personnel Matters), §551.076 (Deliberations regarding Security Devices), §551.086 (Public \nPower Utilities: Competitive Matters), §551.087 (Deliberations regarding Economic Development Negotiations). \n\n4.1.4 CASE NO: JV-2026-011878 of Inspector Stanley Brewer regarding one \n(1) vehicle at 2711 Erskine St. \n \n4.1.5 CASE NO: JV-2026-011962 of Inspector Mike Baker regarding one (1) \nvehicle at 3504 31st St. \n \n4.1.6 CASE NO: JV-2026-012025 of Inspector Courtney Brackeen regarding \none (1) vehicle at 2113 49th St. \n \n4.1.7 CASE NO: JV-2026-012125 of Inspector Chandler Cathey regarding one \n(1) vehicle at 4641 Harvard St. \n \n4.1.8 CASE NO: JV-2026-012127 of Inspector Everest Williams regarding one \n(1) vehicle at 711 E Stanford St. \n \n4.1.9 CASE NO: JV-2026-012129 of Inspector Lisa Lavender regarding one (1) \nvehicle at 2223 39th St. \n \n4.1.10 CASE NO: JV-2026-012333 of Inspector Lisa Lavender regarding one (1) \nvehicle at 2223 39th St. \n \n4.1.11 CASE NO: JV-2026-012390 of Inspector Everest Williams regarding one \n(1) vehicle at 2211 22nd St. \n \n4.1.12 CASE NO: JV-2026-012530 of Inspector Andrew Valenzuela regarding \none (1) vehicle at 2602 E Colgate St. \n \n4.1.13 CASE NO: JV-2026-012540 of Inspector Chandler Cathey regarding one \n(1) vehicle at 4639 Harvard St. \n \n4.1.14 CASE NO: JV-2026-012614 of Inspector Victoria McDonald regarding \none (1) vehicle at 510 51st St. \n \n4.1.15 CASE NO: JV-2026-012632 of Inspector Randy Merrick regarding one \n(1) vehicle at 539 40th St. \n \n4.1.16 CASE NO: JV-2026-012659 of Inspector Dan Tawney regarding one (1) \nvehicle at 15401 Belmont Ave. \n\n4.2 \nWork Session \n \n4.2.1 Procedures for appeal hearings in relation to cases involving Lubbock \nAnimal Services, in accordance with Chapter 4 of the City of Lubbock \nCode of Ordinances. \n\n4.3 \nLubbock Animal Services Appeals \n \n4.3.1 The Permit & License Appeal Board will hear the appeal of Roger Settler \nregarding the decision made by Lubbock Animal Services, declaring a \npublic nuisance at 2120 Broadway Street, in accordance with Chapter 4 of \nthe City of Lubbock Code of Ordinances, and render a decision in \nconnection therewith."}, {"title": "2026-06-17 - Meet and Confer Negotiations - Police (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06172026-93", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "Notice of Open Deliberations Pursuant to Tex. Loc. Gov’t Code § 142.063, this public notice is provided relating to meet and confer deliberations between: City of Lubbock, Texas and Lubbock Professional Police Association Date/Time: June 17, 2026 at 3:00 P.M. Location: Citizens Tower, 2nd Floor Conference Center, 201A/B, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas 79401 Agenda: Deliberations and/o", "text": "Notice of Open Deliberations \nPursuant to Tex. Loc. Gov’t Code § 142.063, this public notice is provided relating to meet and confer \ndeliberations between: \nCity of Lubbock, Texas \nand \nLubbock Professional Police Association \n \nDate/Time: \nJune 17, 2026 at 3:00 P.M. \nLocation: \nCitizens Tower, 2nd Floor Conference Center, 201A/B, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas \n79401 \nAgenda: \nDeliberations and/or related action relating to an agreement or a proposed agreement \nbetween the City of Lubbock, Texas (“City”) and the Lubbock Professional Police \nAssociation (“Association”) as provided for in Texas Local Government Code Chapter \n142, Subchapter B. \nPublic Notice: \nMembers of the public and press are encouraged to observe and monitor the deliberation. A recording of \nthe public portion of the meeting will be made available, but active participation in discussions or \npresentations is expressly prohibited unless permitted by the Ground Rules established by the City and the \nAssociation. \nRepresentatives for either the City or Association may suspend the meeting at any time during the \nproceedings for consultation with their attorney or to have a private caucus with their respective \nrepresentatives. Pursuant to Section 551.071 of the Texas Government Code and Section 142.063(b) of the \nTexas Local Government Code the deliberations during this period are closed to the public \nThe use of cellular phones or sound activated pagers is prohibited while deliberations are being conducted. \nPlease step outside the meeting room should you elect to utilize these devices. \nThis meeting is available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special assistance, please \ncontact the City Secretary's Office at (806)775-2061 or write to Post Office Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas \n79457 at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting."}, {"title": "2026-06-17 - Keep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee 12:00pm (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06172026-94", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "6/10/2026S:\\solid_waste\\Keep Lubbock Beautiful\\Advisory Committee\\0 Meeting Files 0\\Agenda\\2026\\Jun172026.doc Keep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee Agenda June 17, 2026 12:00 p.m. 208 Municipal Dr. 1) Call to Order 2) Citizen Comment – Notice: Any citizen wishing to appear before any regular meeting of the Keep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee shall advise Keep Lubbock Beautiful", "text": "6/10/2026S:\\solid_waste\\Keep Lubbock Beautiful\\Advisory Committee\\0 Meeting Files 0\\Agenda\\2026\\Jun172026.doc \n \nKeep Lubbock Beautiful \nAdvisory Committee Agenda \nJune 17, 2026 12:00 p.m. \n208 Municipal Dr. \n\n1) Call to Order \n\n2) Citizen Comment – Notice: Any citizen wishing to appear before any regular meeting of the Keep Lubbock \nBeautiful Advisory Committee shall advise Keep Lubbock Beautiful of that fact no later than seven calendar \ndays before the meeting at which the citizen wishes to appear. Any citizen wishing to appear shall inform Keep \nLubbock Beautiful, in writing, of the subject of the appearance in sufficient detail. Such notice shall contain the \nname and address of the requestor. The appearance of any citizen giving such notice to Keep Lubbock Beautiful \nshall take precedence in addressing the Keep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee during the Citizen \nComments period. Any citizen failing to advise Keep Lubbock Beautiful of his/her wish to appear before the \nKeep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee as herein above set forth shall, time permitting, be permitted to \naddress the Keep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee after those having given notice. In accordance with \nthe Texas Open Meetings Act, the Keep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee may not take action on public \nmatters during Citizen Comments. \n \n3) Approval of Minutes – May 20, 2026 meeting \n \n4) Work Session \n \na. Beautification Projects \nb. Community Outreach \nc. Lubbock’s Leading Landscapes \nd. Youth Engagement \ne. Programs Review \nf. Review calendar of events \n\nThe above referenced NOTICE OF MEETING posted on the bulletin board outside the east entrance of \nCitizens Tower, 1314 Ave K, Lubbock, Texas, on the _____day of June 2026 at ________ A.M. /P.M. \n\nBy: ____________________________________________________ \n\nKeep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. \nIf you require special assistance, please contact the City of Lubbock at 806-775-3149 or write to P.O. Box \n2000, Lubbock, Texas, 79457, at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting."}, {"title": "2026-06-16 - Transportation Policy Committee 8:30 a.m. (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06162026-91", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "Transportation Policy Committee June 16, 2026, 8:30 a.m. 1314 Avenue K, City Council Chambers Lubbock Texas 79401 1. Call to Order of the Transportation Policy Committee. 2. Acknowledgment of Quorum of the Transportation Policy Committee. 3. Safety Procedures. 4. Public Comment Period/Acknowledgment Opportunity for the public to comment on transportation planning activities.", "text": "Transportation Policy Committee \nJune 16, 2026, 8:30 a.m. \n1314 Avenue K, City Council Chambers \nLubbock Texas 79401 \n \n1. \nCall to Order of the Transportation Policy Committee. \n \n2. \nAcknowledgment of Quorum of the Transportation Policy Committee. \n \n3. \nSafety Procedures. \n \n4. \nPublic Comment Period/Acknowledgment \n \nOpportunity for the public to comment on transportation planning activities. \n \nAction Required: None. \n \n5. \nConsider approval of May 19, 2026, Transportation Policy Committee Meeting minutes \nAction Required: \nConsider approval of the May 19, 2026, Transportation Policy Committee meeting minutes. \nStaff Recommendation: \nApprove. \n \n6. \nReview and Take Action Regarding Grant Development, Grant Application Authority, and Federal \nFunding Strategy \n \nDiscussion: \nStaff will present a summary of currently available and recurring federal funding opportunities \nrelevant to projects identified in the Metropolitan Transportation Plan, 10 Year Plan, Transportation \nImprovement Program, and related multimodal regional priorities. Staff will also discuss the \ncompressed timeframes that now characterize many discretionary grant programs and request \ndirection regarding authority to evaluate, prepare, and submit time sensitive applications when those \napplications are consistent with adopted MPO plans and priorities. \n \nAction Required: \nConsider approval of staff authority to pursue and submit qualifying grant applications and related \nletters of support, subject to subsequent reporting to the Transportation Policy Committee. \n \nStaff Recommendation: \nApproval \n \n7. \nReview and Take Action Regarding MPO Bylaws Review and Creation of a Subcommittee \n \nDiscussion: \nStaff will present an overview of current MPO governance documents, recent state and federal \ncoordination regarding MPO administration, and the need to distinguish between structural \ncompliance items, policy choices, and housekeeping revisions within the bylaws. \n \nAction Required: \nConsider approval to establish a Bylaws subcommittee and direct staff to begin the review process. \n \nStaff Recommendation: \nStaff Recommendation: Approve \n \n8. \nReceive a Report on Renewal and Revision of the Planning Agreement Between TxDOT, the Lubbock \nMetropolitan Planning Organization, and the Fiscal Agent \n\nDiscussion: \nStaff will present an update regarding the draft statewide metropolitan planning agreement, the prior \nextension of the existing agreement, and the need for timely LMPO review and comment before \nreturn to TxDOT. \n \nAction Required: \n Receive Report. \n \n9. \nReview and Take Action Regarding Office Space Procurement and Lease Negotiation Authority \n \nDiscussion: \nStaff will present an update on the current office lease, expiration timing, and the need to evaluate \npublic and private space options for continued MPO operations. Staff requests authority to investigate \noptions, negotiate terms, and return a recommended agreement as appropriate. \n \nAction Required: \nConsider approval authorizing the Executive Director to evaluate office space options, negotiate \nprospective lease terms or extensions, enter and sign a future agreement after returning the \nrecommended agreement to the Transportation Policy Committee as appropriate. \n \nStaff Recommendation: \nStaff Recommendation: Approve \n \n10. \nReports: \nA. Monthly Financial Statement \n \nApril 2026. \n \n11. \nAdjournment \n\nComité de Política de Transporte \n Junio 16, 2026, 8:30 a.m. \n1314 Avenue K, Sala del Ayuntamiento \nLubbock, Texas 79401 \n \n1. \nOrden del Comité de Política de Transporte. \n \n2. \nReconocimiento del quórum del Comité de Política de Transporte. \n \n3. \nProcedimientos de seguridad. \n \n4. \nPeriodo de comentarios públicos/agradecimientos \n \nOportunidad para que el público comente sobre las actividades de planificación del transporte. \n \nAcción requerida: Ninguna. \n \n5. \nConsidere la aprobación de las actas de la reunión del Comité de Política de Transporte del 19 de \nMayo de 2026 \nAcción requerida: \nConsiderar la aprobación de las actas de la reunión del Comité de Política de Transporte del 19 de \nmayo de 2026. \nRecomendación del personal: \n Aprobar. \n \n6. \nRevisar y tomar medidas respecto al desarrollo de subvenciones, la autoridad de solicitud de \nsubvenciones y la estrategia de financiación federal \n \nDiscusión: \nEl personal presentará un resumen de las oportunidades de financiación federal actualmente \ndisponibles y recurrentes relevantes para los proyectos identificados en el Plan Metropolitano de \nTransporte, el Plan Decimal Anual, el Programa de Mejora del Transporte y las prioridades \nregionales multimodales relacionadas. El personal también discutirá los plazos reducidos que ahora \ncaracterizan muchos programas de subvenciones discrecionales y solicitará orientación sobre la \nautoridad para evaluar, preparar y presentar solicitudes sensibles al tiempo cuando dichas \nsolicitudes sean coherentes con los planes y prioridades adoptados de la MPO. \n \nAcción requerida: \nConsidere la aprobación de la autorización del personal para seguir adelante y presentar solicitudes \nde subvención que califican y cartas de apoyo relacionadas, sujetas a posteriores informes al Comité \nde Política de Transporte. \n \nRecomendación del personal: \nAprobadopor \n \n7. \nRevisar y tomar medidas respecto a los Estatutos de la MPO Revisión y creación de un compromiso \nde laSub-c \n \nDiscusión: \nEl personal presentará una visión general de los documentos actuales de gobernanza de la MPO, \nla coordinación reciente entre estado y federal respecto a la administración de la MPO y la necesidad \nde distinguir entre elementos de cumplimiento estructural, elecciones políticas y revisiones de \nmantenimiento dentro de los estatutos. \n \nAcción requerida: \nConsidera la aprobación para establecer un subcomité de la ley y dirige al personal para que \ncomience el proceso de revisión. \n\nRecomendación del personal: \nRecomendación del personal: Aprobar \n \n8. \nRecibir un informe sobre la renovación y revisión del acuerdo de planificación entre TxDOT, la \nOrganización de Planificación Metropolitana de Lubbock y el Agente Fiscal \n \nDiscusión: \nEl personal presentará una actualización sobre el borrador del acuerdo estatal de planificación \nmetropolitana, la prórroga previa del acuerdo existente y la necesidad de una revisión y comentarios \noportunos de la LMPO antes de regresar a TxDOT. \n \nAcción requerida: \n Recibir informe. \n \n9. \nRevisar y tomar medidas respecto a la Autoridad de Adquisición de Espacios de Oficina y Negociación \nde Contratos de Arrendamiento \n \nDiscusión: \nEl personal presentará una actualización sobre el contrato actual de alquiler de oficinas, el plazo de \nexpiración y la necesidad de evaluar opciones de espacios públicos y privados para continuar con \nlas operaciones de la MPO. El personal solicita autoridad para investigar opciones, negociar \ntérminos y devolver un acuerdo recomendado según corresponda. \n \nAcción requerida: \nConsidere la aprobación que autorize al Director Ejecutivo a evaluar opciones de espacio de oficina, \nnegociar posibles términos o extensiones del contrato de alquiler, firmar y firmar un acuerdo futuro \ntras devolver el acuerdo recomendado al Comité de Política de Transporte, según corresponda. \n \nRecomendación del personal: \nRecomendación del personal: Aprobar \n \n10. \nInformes: \nA. Estado financiero mensual \n \nAbril de 2026. \n \n11. \nSuspensión de la sesión"}, {"title": "2026-06-16 - Electric Utility Board Meeting-11:00am (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06162026-90", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "The Electric Utility Board of Lubbock Power & Light Agenda June 16, 2026 11:00 a.m. Edwin “Butch” Davis, P.E., Chair Eddie Schulz, Vice Chair Gwen Stafford, Secretary Dr. Solomon Fields Dr. Gonzalo Ramirez Dr. Craig Rhyne Rhea Hill Mike Stevens Thomas Parker Mark McBrayer, Ex-Officio www.lpandl.com Joel Ivy, Chief Administrative Officer Keli Swan, General Counsel CITIZENS TOWER 1", "text": "The Electric Utility Board of \nLubbock Power & Light Agenda \nJune 16, 2026 \n11:00 a.m. \nEdwin “Butch” Davis, P.E., Chair \nEddie Schulz, Vice Chair \nGwen Stafford, Secretary \nDr. Solomon Fields \nDr. Gonzalo Ramirez \nDr. Craig Rhyne \nRhea Hill \nMike Stevens \nThomas Parker \nMark McBrayer, Ex-Officio \nwww.lpandl.com \nJoel Ivy, Chief Administrative Officer \nKeli Swan, General Counsel \nCITIZENS TOWER \n1314 Ave K \nLubbock, Texas 79401 \nOPEN SESSION: \nCity Council Chambers \nEXECUTIVE SESSION: \nCitizens Tower \nConference Room 201A and 201B \n1.\nCall to Order.\n2.\nPublic Comment. Public comment is an opportunity for the public to make comments and\nexpress a position on agenda items.\na.\nThis period, of up to thirty minutes, is dedicated to public comment. Each member\nof the public will have three minutes to speak. Any member of the public that\nrequires the assistance of a translator will have six minutes to speak. Comments\nmust be limited to only those items posted on the Electric Utility Board agenda.\nAny member of the public wishing to speak shall sign up on the public comment\nsheet on the day of the Electric Utility Board Meeting, prior to the beginning of the\nmeeting. The Electric Utility Board shall follow the order of persons wishing to\nspeak as listed on the sign-up sheet. If everyone who signed up to speak has been\ngiven an opportunity to speak and the time designated for public comment has not\nbeen exhausted, the Electric Utility Board may, at its discretion, open the floor to\nanyone else wishing to address the Electric Utility Board, subject to all the same\nprocedures and guidelines.\n3.\nThe Electric Utility Board may make any comments related to board member activities,\nevents, community engagement, or current or future agenda items.\n1 of 171\n\nExecutive Session \n4.\nHold an executive session in accordance with V.T.C.A. Government Code § 551.086,\n§552.133, and §552.1331 to discuss and deliberate, on the following competitive matters\nof Lubbock Power & Light, reasonably related to the following categories:\n(i) Discussion and deliberation of generation matters, including but not limited to\ngeneration unit and/or portfolio sale opportunities including the potential for unused\nland designated for other uses;\n(ii) Discussion of risk management, contracts, and strategies, customer billing, and usage\ninformation, system load characteristics, and ERCOT power analyses and strategies;\n(iii) Plans, studies, proposals, and analyses for system improvements, additions, or sales\n(other than transmission and distribution system improvements inside the service area\nfor which the public power utility is the sole certificated retail provider);\n(iv) info collected as part of an advanced metering system for usage, services, and billing,\nincluding amounts billed or collected for utility usage\n5.\nHold an executive session in accordance with V.T.C.A. Government Code § 551.071,\nseeking the advice of legal counsel about pending or contemplated litigation or settlement\noffers and hold a consultation with the attorney on matters in which the duty of the attorney\nto the Electric Utility Board under the Texas Disciplinary Rules of Professional Conduct\nof the State Bar of Texas conflicts with Chapter 551 of the Texas Government Code:\n(i)\nlegal advice regarding issues herein listed on the agenda;\n(ii)\nlegal advice and counsel regarding contemplated litigation matters;\n(iii)\nlegal advice and counsel regarding North American Electric Reliability\nCorporation Critical Infrastructure Protection (NERC CIP) standards;\n(iv)\nAjay Mitchell v. City of Lubbock and Lubbock Power and Light, Cause No. DC-\n2025-CV-1728, proceeding in the 72nd District Court of Lubbock County, Texas.\n(v)\nMaria Jesus Tucker v. City of Lubbock and Lubbock Power and Light, Cause No.\nDC-2026-CV-0096, proceeding in the 99th District Court of Lubbock County,\nTexas.\n6. Hold an executive session in accordance with V.T.C.A. Government Code § 551.074(a)(1)\nto deliberate the appointment and/or reappointment of a public officer or employee\n(Electric Utility Board).\n7. Hold an executive session in accordance with V.T.C.A. Government Code § 551.074(a)(1)\nto deliberate the appointment, employment, evaluation, and duties of a public officer or\nemployee (Director of Electric Utilities/Chief Administrative Officer).\n2 of 171\nBack to Agenda\n\n11:30 a.m. – Approximately - Following completion of the Executive Session, the Electric \nUtility Board will reconvene in open session to discuss the items listed below. It is anticipated \nthat the open session will begin at 11:30 a.m. However, this is an approximation, and the \nBoard may begin the open session earlier or later depending on when the Executive Session is \ncomplete. \nOpen Session \n8.\nApprove the minutes from the Regular Electric Utility Board meeting held on May 19,\n2026.\n9.\nPresentation and discussion of the update/report by the LP&L Chief Administrative\nOfficer, or his designee, regarding strategic planning, board committee reports, association\nmatters, ordinance change requests, EUB policy and procedures, customer service,\nbusiness center practices, procedures and policies, transition to retail customer choice,\ncustomer concerns and complaints, billing system, forms and procedures, status of\ntransmission and distribution projects, generation, mutual aid, weather events, outage and\nrestoration efforts, grid matters, Electric Reliability Council of Texas (“ERCOT”) matters\nand committee participation, staffing levels, personnel, regulatory matters, training,\ncybersecurity, mutual aid agreement, and operational performance metrics.\n10.\nPresentation and discussion of financial and capital statements, budget, financing options,\naudits, and financial policies of Lubbock Power & Light relating to debt issuance issues\nand historical debt matters, reserve account funding, cost allocation, revenue and expense\nprojections, customer metering, tariff and billing, service and administrative issues, and\nrisk management information including rates.\nConsent \n11.\nConsider a resolution authorizing the Chief Administrative Officer, or his designee to\nexecute a contract to The Big Red for grant consulting services. The contract is a six-\nmonth term with retainer fees not to exceed $150,000.00 and an additional one-time\nperformance fee of five (5) percent of grant awarded funds.\n12.\nConsider a resolution authorizing the Chief Administrative Officer or his designee to\nexecute an engagement with Valkenaar & O’Donnell PLLC regarding Tucker v. City of\nLubbock and Lubbock Power & Light and ongoing governance issues for LP&L.\n13.\nConsider a resolution recommending that the City Council of Lubbock authorize the Chief\nAdministrative Officer or his designee to execute a contract for the Purchase and Sale of\nTy Cooke Gas Generating Facility in the amount of $9.25 million, pursuant to RFP 7107-\n25-EUA.\n14.\nConsider a resolution authorizing the LP&L Chief Administrative Officer or his designee\nto execute a First Amendment to Professional Services Agreement, by and between the\n3 of 171\nBack to Agenda\n\nCity of Lubbock, acting by and through LP&L, and Baker Tilly US, LLP, and Illinois \nCompany, for assistance with writing applications for competitive grants and other \nassociated needs. This amendment will extend the term for one additional year. \n15.\nConsider a resolution authorizing the LP&L Chief Administrative Officer or his designee\nto execute a First Amendment to Professional Services Agreement which is set to expire\non July 16, 2026, by and between the City of Lubbock, acting by and through LP&L, and\nTexHahn Media, Inc. (d.b.a. Hahn), for communication and marketing services. This\namendment will extend term for an additional one-year term.\n16.\nConsider a resolution authorizing the LP&L Chief Administrative Officer or his designee\nto execute a First Amendment to Professional Services Agreement dated which is set to\nexpire on July 16, 2026, by and between the City of Lubbock, acting by and through LP&L,\nand Hillco Partners, LLC, for continued legislative support and communications services.\nThis amendment extends the term of the Agreement by one year and increases the Not-to-\nExceed from $150,000.00 to $250,000.00.\n17.\nConsider a resolution authorizing the Purchasing Manager, or his designee, to execute\nPurchase Order, by and between the City of Lubbock, acting by and through Lubbock\nPower & Light, and Kirby Smith Machinery Inc., of Lubbock, Texas, BuyBoard contract\n788-25. This BuyBoard quote for $478,800.00 will be for an additional TSE four drum\nelectric puller that will assist our distribution crews to pull multiple energized conductor at\nonce as approved in the FY 2025-26 Fleet Capital Program budget.\n18.\nConsider a resolution rejecting all bids for Request for Proposal (RFP) 7117-26-ELD -\nLP&L 350 MVA Autotransformers. Quantities required for this RFP will be reduced and\na new RFP will be submitted with updated evaluation criteria.\n19.\nAdjourn.\nTHE ELECTRIC UTILITY BOARD RESERVES THE RIGHT TO ADJOURN INTO EXECUTIVE SESSION AS AUTHORIZED BY \nTEX. GOV’T CODE § 551.001, ET. SEQ. (THE TEXAS OPEN MEETINGS ACT) ON ANY ITEM ON ITS OPEN MEETING AGENDA \nOR TO RECONVENE IN A CONTINUATION OF THE EXECUTIVE SESSION ON THE EXECUTIVE SESSION ITEMS NOTED \nABOVE, IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE TEXAS OPEN MEETINGS ACT, INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION §§ 551.071-551.086. \nPosted on the bulletin board outside the south \nentrance \nof \nCitizens \nTower, \n1314 \nAve. \nK., Lubbock, Texas, on the 1 0 th June 2026, \nat 10:30A.M.\nBy:______________________________ \nCITY OF LUBBOCK ELECTRIC UTILITY BOARD MEETINGS ARE AVAILABLE TO ALL PERSONS REGARDLESS OF DISABILITY. IF YOU \nREQUIRE SPECIAL ASSISTANCE, PLEASE CONTACT THE CITY SECRETARY AT (806)775-2026 OR WRITE P. O. BOX 2000, LUBBOCK, \nXAS 79457, AT LEAST 48 HOURS IN ADVANCE OF THE MEETING. \n4 of 171\nBeatrice Duenez\nBack to Agenda\n\nThe Electric Utility Board of \nLubbock Power & Light \nMinutes\n May 19, 2026 \n11:00 a.m. \nEdwin “Butch” Davis, P.E., Chair \nEddie Schulz, Vice Chair \nGwen Stafford, Secretary \nDr. Solomon Fields \nDr. Gonzalo Ramirez \nDr. Craig Rhyne \nRhea Hill \nMike Stevens \nThomas Parker \nMark McBrayer, Ex-Officio \nwww.lpandl.com \nJoel Ivy, Chief Administrative Officer \nKeli Swan, General Counsel \nCITIZENS TOWER \n1314 Ave K \nLubbock, Texas 79401 \nOPEN SESSION: \nCity Council Chambers \nEXECUTIVE SESSION: \nCitizens Tower \nCouncil Workroom 101A \nEUB \nCity Staff \nLP&L Staff \nJoel Ivy \nGwen Stafford \nButch Davis \nJarrett Atkinson \nMatt Wade \nKeli Swan \nClint Gardner \nDr. Gonzalo Ramirez \nRhea Hill \nThomas Parker \nMike Stevens \nEddie Schulz \nDr. Solomon Fields \nDr. Craig Rhyne \nBeatrice Duenez \nCady Mello \nBlair McGinnis \nKacey Johnson \nMatt Rose \nTina Cooper \nClint Gardner \nSkylar Borunda \nCity Council \nMark McBrayer \nTim Collins \nChristy-Martinez-Garcia \nJeff Baker \nRenee Treat \nKody Morris \nHarvey Hall \nRachel Hendrix \nMichael Winegeart \nTamara Randles \nDaniel Garcia \nMarty Muniz \nCamille Powe \nAmy Day \n5 of 171\nBack to Agenda\n\n1.\nCall to Order.\nBoard Chair Butch Davis called the meeting to order at 11:00 a.m.\nThe Board and LP&L Staff took group photos and returned at 11:09 a.m.\n2.\nPublic Comment. Public comment is an opportunity for the public to make comments and\nexpress a position on agenda items.\na.\nThis period, of up to thirty minutes, is dedicated to public comment. Each member\nof the public will have three minutes to speak. Any member of the public that\nrequires the assistance of a translator will have six minutes to speak. Comments\nmust be limited to only those items posted on the Electric Utility Board agenda.\nAny member of the public wishing to speak shall sign up on the public comment\nsheet on the day of the Electric Utility Board Meeting, prior to the beginning of the\nmeeting. The Electric Utility Board shall follow the order of persons wishing to\nspeak as listed on the sign-up sheet. If everyone who signed up to speak has been\ngiven an opportunity to speak and the time designated for public comment has not\nbeen exhausted, the Electric Utility Board may, at its discretion, open the floor to\nanyone else wishing to address the Electric Utility Board, subject to all the same\nprocedures and guidelines.\nNo public comments.\n3.\nThe Electric Utility Board may make any comments related to board member activities,\nevents, community engagement, or current or future agenda items.\nChair Davis commented that each Board member was provided with a list of committee\nmembers and updated contact lists. Board Member Thomas Parker commented on an\nevent run by Councilwoman Christy Martinez-Garcia and congratulated her on winning\nan award.\nExecutive Session \nThe Board recessed into executive session at 11:11 a.m. \nAshley Busch \nColby Morris \nNoah Henry \nQuincy Gutierrez \nErich Von Heuval \n6 of 171\nBack to Agenda\n\n4. \nHold an executive session in accordance with V.T.C.A. Government Code § 551.086, \n§552.133, and §552.1331 to discuss and deliberate, on the following competitive matters \nof Lubbock Power & Light, reasonably related to the following categories: \n \n(i) Discussion and deliberation of generation matters, including but not limited to \ngeneration unit and/or portfolio sale opportunities including the potential for unused \nland designated for other uses; \n \n(ii) Discussion of risk management, contracts, and strategies, customer billing, and usage \ninformation, system load characteristics, and ERCOT power analyses and strategies; \n \n(iii) Plans, studies, proposals, and analyses for system improvements, additions, or sales \n(other than transmission and distribution system improvements inside the service area \nfor which the public power utility is the sole certificated retail provider); \n \n(iv) info collected as part of an advanced metering system for usage, services, and billing, \nincluding amounts billed or collected for utility usage \n \n5. \nHold an executive session in accordance with V.T.C.A. Government Code § 551.071, \nseeking the advice of legal counsel about pending or contemplated litigation or settlement \noffers and hold a consultation with the attorney on matters in which the duty of the attorney \nto the Electric Utility Board under the Texas Disciplinary Rules of Professional Conduct \nof the State Bar of Texas conflicts with Chapter 551 of the Texas Government Code: \n \n(i) \nlegal advice regarding issues herein listed on the agenda; \n(ii) \nlegal advice and counsel regarding contemplated litigation matters; \n(iii) \nlegal advice and counsel regarding North American Electric Reliability \nCorporation Critical Infrastructure Protection (NERC CIP) standards; \n \n(iv) \nAjay Mitchell v. City of Lubbock and Lubbock Power and Light, Cause No. DC-\n2025-CV-1728, proceeding in the 72nd District Court of Lubbock County, Texas. \n \n(v) \nMaria Jesus Tucker v. City of Lubbock and Lubbock Power and Light, Cause No. \nDC-2026-CV-0096, proceeding in the 99th District Court of Lubbock County, \nTexas. \n \n6. Hold an executive session in accordance with V.T.C.A. Government Code § 551.074(a)(1) \nto deliberate the appointment and/or reappointment of a public officer or employee \n(Electric Utility Board). \n \n7. Hold an executive session in accordance with V.T.C.A. Government Code § 551.074(a)(1) \nto deliberate the appointment, employment, evaluation, and duties of a public officer or \nemployee (Director of Electric Utilities/Chief Administrative Officer, and General \nCounsel). \n\n7 of 171\nBack to Agenda\n\nOpen Session \nThe Board reconvened in open session at 1:19 p.m. \n8.\nApprove the minutes from the Regular Electric Utility Board meeting held on April 21,\n2026.\nVice-Chair Eddie Schulz made a motion to pass the minutes, which was seconded by\nBoard Member Thomas Parker. The Board approved the minutes by a vote of 9-0.\nLP&L General Counsel Keli Swan introduced LP&L’s new Assistant In-House\nCounsel, Cady Mello. LP&L Chief Operating Officer Blair McGinnis introduced\nLP&L’s new engineering manager, Colby Morris. LP&L Director of Finance Kacey\nJohnson introduced LP&L’s new buyer, Quincy Gutierrez, and senior accountant,\nNoah Henry.\n9.\nPresentation and discussion of the update/report by the LP&L Chief Administrative\nOfficer, or his designee, regarding strategic planning, board committee reports, association\nmatters, ordinance change requests, EUB policy and procedures, customer service,\nbusiness center practices, procedures and policies, transition to retail customer choice,\ncustomer concerns and complaints, billing system, forms and procedures, status of\ntransmission and distribution projects, generation, mutual aid, weather events, outage and\nrestoration efforts, grid matters, Electric Reliability Council of Texas (“ERCOT”) matters\nand committee participation, staffing levels, personnel, regulatory matters, training,\ncybersecurity, mutual aid agreement, and operational performance metrics.\nLP&L Chief Performance Officer Renee Treat presented the Board with LP&L’s\nperformance improvement strategy, including tasks and goals. Ms. Treat described how\nLP&L is working towards organizational improvement with a large focus on leadership.\n10.\nPresentation and discussion of financial and capital statements, budget, financing options,\naudits, and financial policies of Lubbock Power & Light relating to debt issuance issues\nand historical debt matters, reserve account funding, cost allocation, revenue and expense\nprojections, customer metering, tariff and billing, service and administrative issues, and\nrisk management information including rates.\nDirector of Finance Johnson presented LP&L’s March financial statements.\nConsent \nConsent items 11-15 were considered. \n8 of 171\nBack to Agenda\n\nA motion to approve all consent items was made by Board Member Dr. Gonzalo \nRamirez and seconded by Vice-Chair Eddie Schulz. The motion to approve was passed \nby vote of 9-0. \n11.\nConsider a resolution authorizing the Chief Administrative Officer or his designee to\nexecute a Professional Services Agreement (Agreement) by and between the City of\nLubbock, acting by and through Lubbock Power & Light, for Independent Representative\n(Owner’s Engineering) Services with Electrical Consultants, Inc. (ECI). This will be a four-\nyear agreement with a not-to-exceed of Five Million, Two Hundred Thousand Dollars and\nzero/100 dollars ($5,200,000.00).\n12.\nConsider a resolution authorizing the Chief Administrative Officer, or his designee, to\nexecute Professional Service Agreement by and between the City of Lubbock, acting by\nand through Lubbock Power & Light, and 1898 and Co., of Kansas City, Missouri, Request\nfor Proposal (RFP) 7105-26-ELD - LP&L Operations Software Implementation Program\nConsulting Services. This agreement for $1,590,000.00 ELD - LP&L Operations Software\nImplementation Program Consulting Services. This agreement for $1,590,000.00 includes\nchange order language of up to 20% of the NTE may be authorized by the Chief\nAdministrative Officer, notwithstanding his purchasing authority will be for a term of 36\nmonths with the option to extend an additional two (2) one-year extensions of time so long\nas the amount of the consideration payable hereunder does not increase. This agreement\nincludes professional and project management services, guidance and oversight for\nGeographic Information System (GIS) upgrade, implementation of a new Work Asset\nManagement System, and the implementation of a new Advanced Distribution\nManagement System (ADMS).\n13.\nConsider a resolution appointing and authorizing the Chief Administrative Officer to act\nas the Authorized Representative for all Lubbock Power & Light filings with the Electric\nReliability Council of Texas, appointing and authorizing the Chief Operating Officer and\nthe Chief Compliance Officer to act as the Back-up Authorized Representative(s), and\nsuperseding and replacing Resolution No. EUB 2025-R0007 regarding the previous\nAuthorized Representative and Back-up Authorized Representative for ERCOT.\n14.\nConsider a resolution authorizing the Purchasing Manager, or his designee, to "}, {"title": "2026-06-15 - Valencia Public Improvement District Advisory Board Regular Meeting - 10:00 AM (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06152026-84", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "The above referenced NOTICE OF MEETING was posted outside the South entrance of Citizens Tower, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas, on the _____ day of ______________, 2026 at___________ A.M/P.M. _________________________________________ Jon Jackson, Chair Stephanie Brown Chrystal Jansz Rieken James Jordan Corey Lusk Valencia Public Improvement District Advisory Board Regular Meeting Agenda", "text": "The above referenced NOTICE OF MEETING was posted outside the South entrance of Citizens Tower, 1314 Avenue \nK, Lubbock, Texas, on the _____ day of ______________, 2026 at___________ A.M/P.M. \n_________________________________________ \n \nJon Jackson, Chair \nStephanie Brown \nChrystal Jansz Rieken \nJames Jordan \nCorey Lusk \n\nValencia Public Improvement District Advisory Board \nRegular Meeting Agenda \nJune 15, 2026 | 10:00 A.M. \n \nTeams Link: \nhttps://teams.microsoft.com/meet/260250110429583?p=Bmq1op7DjfNECzQS6n \nMeeting ID: 260 250 110 429 583 Passcode: rb7QL2z7 \n \nMolly Ballesteros, Special \nDistricts Manager \nDanielle Williams, Business \nDevelopment Director \n\nValencia Public Improvement District Advisory Board meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you \nrequire \nspecial \nassistance, \nplease \ncontact \nthe \nBusiness \nDevelopment \nDepartment \nat \n806.775.3083, \ne-mail \nbusinessdevelopment@mylubbock.us, or write to Post Office Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas 79457 at least 48 hours in advance of \nthe meeting. \n \n1. \nCall to order \n \n2. \nCitizen Comments - Any citizen wishing to address the Valencia Public Improvement District Advisory Board, \nmay submit a citizen comment by email at businessdevelopment@mylubbock.us no later than 5 p.m. on the date \nbefore the meeting. Submitted comments must include name and address. Citizen Comments is an opportunity \nfor citizens to make comments and express a position on agenda items. Each comment will be read aloud for a \nperiod of time not to exceed three minutes pursuant to City Council rules. Any comment received that is in the \nnature of asking a question will be referred to an appropriate member of the City staff for a response. \n \n3. \nFinancial Report \n \n4. \nRegular Session \n \n4.1 \nApproval of Minutes – January 21, 2026, January 27, 2026, & March 6, 2026 \n \n4.2 \nDiscuss and take appropriate action on the Fiscal Year 2026-27 Service and Assessment Plan \n \n4.3 \nDiscuss and take appropriate action on a Proposal for Park Aeration Services \n\n5. \nWork Session \n \n5.1 \nLandscape Maintenance Discussion \n \n5.2 \n2026 Annual Property Owner Meeting Discussion \n \n6. \nSchedule Next Meeting – The suggested next meeting date is September 17, 2026, at 1:00 p.m."}, {"title": "2026-06-12 - North Point Public Improvement District Advisory Board Regular Meeting - 3:00 PM (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06122026-86", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "The a