an appropriate member of the City staff for a response and will not be \nread aloud at the meeting. \n \n3. \nFinancial Report \n \n4. \nRegular Session \n \n4.1 \nApproval of Minutes – March 13, 2026 \n \n4.2 \nDiscuss and take appropriate action on a Tom’s Tree Place proposal to install \nBermuda Grass at the West Walking Track \n \n4.3 \nDiscuss and take appropriate action on a Change Order to the Tom’s Tree Place \nLandscape Maintenance Contract \n \n4.4 \nDiscuss and take appropriate action on the Fiscal Year 2026-27 Service and \nAssessment Plan \n \n5. \nWork Session \n \n5.1 \n2026 Annual Property Owner Meeting Discussion \n \n6. \nSchedule Next Meeting – The suggested next meeting date is September 18, 2026, at 3:00 p.m."}, {"title": "2026-06-12 - Bell Farms Public Improvement District Advisory Board Regular Meeting - 1:30PM (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06122026-85", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "Trace Moore, Chair Francisco Avila, Vice Chair Jennifer Roseberry James Smith Bell Farms Public Improvement District Advisory Board Regular Meeting Agenda June 12, 2026 |1:30 P.M. Teams Link: https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/268137558344594?p=JJkBJpI5ulkQRjgRLc Meeting ID: 268 137 558 344 594 Passcode: Ks6cS2hD Molly Ballesteros, Special Districts Manager Danielle Williams, Busin", "text": "Trace Moore, Chair \nFrancisco Avila, Vice Chair \nJennifer Roseberry \nJames Smith \n\nBell Farms Public Improvement District Advisory Board \nRegular Meeting Agenda \n June 12, 2026 |1:30 P.M. \n \nTeams Link: \nhttps://teams.microsoft.com/meet/268137558344594?p=JJkBJpI5ulkQRjgRLc \nMeeting ID: 268 137 558 344 594 Passcode: Ks6cS2hD \n \nMolly Ballesteros, Special \nDistricts Manager \nDanielle Williams, Business \nDevelopment Director \nBell Farms Public Improvement District Advisory Board meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you \nrequire \nspecial \nassistance, \nplease \