 comments must include name and address. Citizen \nComments is an opportunity for citizens to make comments and express a position on agenda items. Each \ncomment will be read aloud for a period of time not to exceed three minutes pursuant to City Council rules. \nAny comment received that is in the nature of asking a question will be referred to an appropriate member \nof the City staff for a response. \n \n3. \nFinancial Report \n \n4. \nRegular Session \n \n4.1 \nApproval of Minutes – February 5, 2026 \n \n4.2 \nDiscuss and take appropriate action on the Fiscal Year 2026-27 Service and Assessment Plan \n \n4.3 \nDiscuss and take appropriate action on Park Stormwater Drainage Improvement Project \nContract \n \n4.4 \nDiscuss and take appropriate action on a Sports Court Fence Repair Proposal from Tom’s \nTree Place \n \n4.5 \nDiscuss and take appropriate action on a Sports Court Remediation Proposal from Tom’s \nTree Place \n \n5. \nWork Session \n \n5.1 \n2026 Annual Property Owner Meeting Discussion \n \n6. \nSchedule Next Meeting – The suggested next meeting date is April 30, 2026 at 3:30 p.m."}, {"title": "2026-06-10 - The Lubbock Fire Pension Fund Board of Trustees will conduct a regular meeting on Wednesday, June 10, 2026 at 1:00 p.m. in the City Bank Conference Room. (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06102026-81", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "NOTICE OF A REGULAR MEETING OF THE LUBBOCK FIRE PENSION FUND BOARD OF TRUSTEES The Lubbock Fire Pension Fund Board of Trustees will conduct a regular meeting on Wednesday, June 10, 2026 at 1:00 p.m. in the City Bank Conference Room, located at 611 University Avenue, Lubbock, TX 79401, for the purposes set forth in the following agenda: AGENDA Discussion and Action may be taken on the followi", "text": "NOTICE OF A REGULAR MEETING OF THE \nLUBBOCK FIRE PENSION FUND \nBOARD OF TRUSTEES \nThe Lubbock Fire Pension Fund Board of Trustees will conduct a regular meeting on Wednesday, June 10, 2026 at 1:00 p.m. in the City \nBank Conference Room, located at 611 University Avenue, Lubbock, TX 79401, for the purposes set forth in the following agenda: \nAGENDA \nDiscussion and Action may be taken on the following items: \n1.\nCall to Order \n2.\nPublic Comment – Any member of the public wishing to address the Lubbock Fire Pension Fund Board, regarding any matter on\nthe Agenda shall email lubbockfire@lauterbachamen.com by 11:00 a.m. on the day of the Board meeting. Comments by any\nindividual may not exceed five minutes in length unless extended by the Chairman. \n3.\nBenefit Applications, Changes, and QDROs (Qualified Domestic Relations Order) \n4.\nConsent Agenda – All matters listed under the Consent Agenda, are considered routine by the Board and will be enacted by one\nmotion. These include authorization of payment expenses. There will not be separate discussion of these items. If any Trustee \ndesires to discuss an item on the Consent Agenda, it will be moved to the Regular agenda for further consideration. \na)\nMay 13, 2026 Board Meeting Minutes \nb)\nLauterbach & Amen invoice in the amount of $7,515 for April 2026 professional services \nc)\nStephanie Masson in the amount of $609.98 for pension office printer replacement purchase \nd)\nJackson Walker LLP invoice in the amount of $14,904 for February 2026 legal services rendered \n5.\nConsultant Presentation by CAPTRUST \na)\nPreliminary May 2026 Performance\nb)\nDiscussion and Possible Action on Fund Rebalancing Recommendations \n6.\nOld Business \na)\nDiscussion and Possible Action on Plan Document Update \n7.\nNew Business \n8.\nAdministrator’s Report \na)\nMonthly Financial Report \nb)\nDemographics \nc)\nInvestments Update \nd)\nOffice Update \ne)\nTrustee Training \n9.\nCommittee Reports \na)\nMembership Committee \nb)\nLegislative Committee \nc)\nNominations Committee \nd)\nInvestments Committee \n10.\nAdjournment \nThe next regular meeting is scheduled for Wednesday, July 8, 2026 at 1:00 p.m. \nPosted: June 4, 2026 \nBy: Elizabeth Adelmann \nCity of Lubbock Fire Pension Fund Board Meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special assistance, \nplease contact Elizabeth Adelmann at (630) 821-0201 at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting."}, {"title": "2026-06-10 - Community Development Services Board Public Hearing Meeting (Minutes)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Minutes/_06102026-82", "category": "Minutes", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "Community Development & Services Board (CDSB) Regular Meeting Minutes April 8, 2026 at 5:30 p.m. 1708 Crickets Ave. Members Present Staff Present Marcella Ford Aimee George Brenda Hawkins Nitra Barnes Maria Gomez Milton Lee Karen Murfee David Robertson Dustie Delashaw Corina Gonzales Board convened at 5:40 p.m. There was a quorum. Citizen comment: Jaliyah Jackson – listeni", "text": "Community Development & Services Board (CDSB) \nRegular Meeting Minutes \nApril 8, 2026 at 5:30 p.m. \n1708 Crickets Ave. \n \nMembers Present \n \nStaff Present \nMarcella Ford \nAimee George \nBrenda Hawkins \nNitra Barnes \nMaria Gomez \nMilton Lee \n\nKaren Murfee \nDavid Robertson \n \nDustie Delashaw \nCorina Gonzales \n\nBoard convened at 5:40 p.m. There was a quorum. \nCitizen comment: Jaliyah Jackson – listening only \nAction Items: \n1.1 Approved Minutes – A motion was made by Brenda, 2nd by Nitra to approve minutes from the March \n11, 2026 CDSB meeting. Motion Carried \nWork Session: \n2.1 Discussed 2026 Calendar, Annual Action Plan, part of 5 year plan. CAPER due 12/29/2026 \n2.2 Discussed PY2026-2027 Funding \n \nThe meeting adjourned at 5:53 p.m. \nNext CDSB meeting scheduled for May 13, 2026 at 5:30 p.m. \n\nBoard Chair \n\n Date \n\nBoard Secretary \n\n Date"}, {"title": "2026-06-09 - Upland Crossing Public Improvement District Advisory Board Regular Meeting (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06092026-83", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "The above referenced NOTICE OF MEETING was posted outside the South entrance of Citizens Tower, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas, on the _____ day of ____________, 2026 at________A.M./P.M. ___________________________________ Austin Lear, Chair Trey Benton, Vice Chair Jordan Rodgers Jennifer Tollett Upland Crossing Public Improvement District Advisory Board Regular Meeting Agenda June 9,", "text": "The above referenced NOTICE OF MEETING was posted outside the South entrance of Citizens Tower, 1314 \nAvenue K, Lubbock, Texas, on the _____ day of ____________, 2026 at________A.M./P.M. \n\n ___________________________________ \n\nAustin Lear, Chair \nTrey Benton, Vice Chair \nJordan Rodgers \nJennifer Tollett \n\nUpland Crossing Public Improvement District \nAdvisory Board Regular Meeting Agenda \n June 9, 2026 | 11:30 A.M. \nMicrosoft Teams Link: \nhttps://teams.microsoft.com/meet/24753043958185?p=DtzuOcUWIOhZqs2D6N \nMeeting ID: 247 530 439 581 85 Passcode: rX7tX7gX \n \nMolly Ballesteros, \nSpecial Districts Manager \nDanielle Williams, \nBusiness Development \nDirector \n\nUpland Crossing Public Improvement District meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special \nassistance, please contact the Business Development Department at 806.775.3083, e-mail businessdevelopment@mylubbock.us, or \nwrite to Post Office Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas 79457 at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting. \n \n1. \nCall to order \n \n2. \nCitizen Comments - Any citizen wishing to address the Upland Crossing Public Improvement \nDistrict \nAdvisory \nBoard, \nmay \nsubmit \na \ncitizen \ncomment \nby \nemail \nat \nbusinessdevelopment@mylubbock.us no later than 5 p.m. on the date before the meeting. \nSubmitted comments must include name and address. Citizen Comments is an opportunity for \ncitizens to make comments and express a position on agenda items. Each comment will be read \naloud for a period of time not to exceed three minutes pursuant to City Council rules. Any comment \nreceived that is in the nature of asking a question will be referred to an appropriate member of the \nCity staff for a response. \n \n3. \nFinancial Report \n \n4. \nRegular Session \n \n4.1 \nApproval of Minutes \nOctober 21, 2025 \nJanuary 6, 2026 \nFebruary 13, 2026 \nMarch 11, 2026 \n \n4.2 \nDiscuss and take appropriate action on the Fiscal Year 2026-27 Service and \nAssessment Plan \n \n5. \nWork Session \n \n5.1 \nPlaya Lake Park Stormwater Drainage Remediation Project Update \n \n5.2 \n2026 Annual Property Owner Meeting Discussion \n \n6. \nSchedule Next Meeting – The next proposed meeting day is August 4, 2026, at 11:30 a.m."}, {"title": "2026-06-09 - Lubbock Animal Services Advisory Board - 11:30 AM (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06092026-72", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "Animal Services Advisory Board Regular Meeting Agenda June 9, 2026 11:30 a.m. 1306 9th Street Lubbock Public Library – Mahon Branch 1. CALL TO ORDER 2. CITIZEN COMMENTS – According to Lubbock Animal Services Advisory Board Rules, any citizens wishing to appear in-person before a regular meeting of the Advisory Board, regarding any matter posted on the Advisory Board Agenda below, shall", "text": "Animal Services Advisory Board \nRegular Meeting Agenda \nJune 9, 2026 \n11:30 a.m. \n1306 9th Street \nLubbock Public Library – Mahon Branch \n\n1. CALL TO ORDER \n \n2. CITIZEN COMMENTS – According to Lubbock Animal Services Advisory Board Rules, \nany citizens wishing to appear in-person before a regular meeting of the Advisory Board, \nregarding any matter posted on the Advisory Board Agenda below, shall complete the sign-\nup form provided at the meeting, no later than 11:30 a.m. on June 9, 2026. Citizen Comments \nprovide an opportunity for citizens to make comments and express a position on the agenda \nitems. Citizen comments will be limited to 3 minutes each. \n \n3. APPROVAL OF APRIL 14, 2026, MEETING MINUTES \n \n4. WORK SESSION DIRECTOR’S REPORT \n \n4.1 Staffing \n4.2 Operations \n4.2.1 \nBite Reporting FY 25/26 \n4.3 Performance Metrics \n4.4 Events \n \n5. GENERAL DISCUSSION \n \n6. DATE AND TIME OF NEXT MEETING \n \n7. ADJOURN \n \nThe above-referenced NOTICE OF MEETING was posted on the bulletin board outside the south entrance \nof Citizens Tower, 1314 Ave K, Lubbock, Texas, on the ___ day __________________ at ______AM/PM. \nBy: _____________________________________ \n \nAnimal Services Advisory Board meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you \nrequire special assistance, please contact the City of Lubbock at 806-775-2710 or write to P.O. Box \n2000, Lubbock, Texas, 79401, at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting."}, {"title": "2026-06-09 - June 9, 2026 Regular City Council Meeting (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06092026-80", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "City of Lubbock, Texas Regular City Council Meeting June 9, 2026 Mark W. McBrayer, Mayor Dr. Jennifer Wilson, Mayor Pro Tem, District 5 Christy Martinez-Garcia, District 1 Gordon Harris, Councilman, District 2 David Bruegel, Councilman, District 3 Brayden Rose, Councilman, District 4 Tim Collins, Councilman, District 6 W. Jarrett Atkinson, City Manager Matt Wade, City Attorney Courtney Paz, City", "text": "City of Lubbock, Texas\nRegular City Council Meeting\nJune 9, 2026\nMark W. McBrayer, Mayor\nDr. Jennifer Wilson, Mayor Pro Tem, District 5\nChristy Martinez-Garcia, District 1\nGordon Harris, Councilman, District 2\nDavid Bruegel, Councilman, District 3\nBrayden Rose, Councilman, District 4\nTim Collins, Councilman, District 6\n \nW. Jarrett Atkinson, City Manager\nMatt Wade, City Attorney\nCourtney Paz, City Secretary\nhttp://www.mylubbock.us\nCity Council Chambers, Citizens Tower, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas\n \nCity of Lubbock City Council Meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special assistance, please contact\nthe City Secretary's Office at (806)775-2061 or write to Post Office Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas 79457 at least 48 hours in advance of the\nmeeting. \nExecutive Session Disclosure Statement: The City Council reserves the right to adjourn into executive session at any time during the course of\nthe meeting to discuss any item listed on this agenda as authorized by Chapter 551 of the Texas Government Code, including but not\nnecessarily limited to §551.071 (Consultation with Attorney), §551.072 (Deliberations regarding Real Property), §551.073 (Deliberations\nregarding Gifts and Donations), §551.074 (Personnel Matters), §551.076 (Deliberations regarding Security Devices), §551.086 (Public\nPower Utilities: Competitive Matters), §551.087 (Deliberations regarding Economic Development Negotiations). \nA quorum of the City Council will be physically present in City Council Chambers located in Citizens Tower, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas,\nas it is the intent of the City Council to have a quorum physically present at this location. One or more members of the City Council, however,\nmay participate in the meeting by video-conference call as permitted under Section 551.127 of the Texas Government Code. \nNote: On occasion, the City Council may consider agenda items out of order. \n. \n \n1:30 p.m. - City Council convenes in City Council Chambers and immediately recesses into Executive Session.\n\n1.\nExecutive Session\n \n1. 1.\nHold an executive session in accordance with the Texas Government Code, Section 551.072, to\ndeliberate the purchase, exchange, lease, or value of real property. \n \n1. 1. 1.\nLubbock Riverwalk, LLC\n \nAdjourn from Executive Session\n \nImmediately following Executive Session, the City Council reconvenes in City Council Chambers in Work\nSession.\n \n2.\nHear and discuss presentations regarding the following and provide guidance to staff as appropriate. \n\n2. 1.\nPresentation - Texas State Comptroller's Office Transparency Star Award - Traditional Finances \n \n2. 2.\nPresentation of a Special Recognition for Responsible Fatherhood Month \n \n2:00 p.m. - City Council continues in Open Session in City Council Chambers.\n \n3.\nCeremonial Items\n \n3. 1.\nInvocation \n \n3. 2.\nPledges of Allegiance \n \nCall to Order\n \n4.\nCitizen Comments - According to Lubbock City Council Rules, any citizen wishing to appear\nin-person before a regular meeting of the City Council, regarding any matter posted on the City\nCouncil Agenda below, shall complete the sign-up form provided at the meeting, no later than\n2:00 p.m. on June 9, 2026. Citizen Comments provide an opportunity for citizens to make\ncomments and express a position on agenda items.\n \n5.\nMinutes\n \n5. 1.\nMay 12, 2026 Regular City Council Meeting\nMay 20, 2026 Special City Council Meeting - Swearing-In Ceremony \n \n6.\nConsent Agenda - Items considered to be routine are enacted by one motion without separate\ndiscussion. If the City Council desires to discuss an item, the item is removed from the Consent\nAgenda and considered separately.\n \n6. 1.\nBudget Ordinance Amendment 2nd Reading - Finance: Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0062,\namending Section IV of Budget Amendment 18, to the FY 2025-26 Budget for municipal purposes,\nrespecting the transfer from the Airport Operating Fund to the Airport Capital Project Fund, correcting\na clerical error. \n \n6. 2.\nBudget Ordinance Amendment 1st Reading - Finance: Consider Budget Ordinance Amendment 30,\nrespecting the General Fund and Grant Fund in connection with accepting grant funding from the Texas\nDepartment of State Health Services, for the Texas Spay and Neuter Program Grant Fund. \n \n6. 3.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Right-of-Way: Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0066, and related\ndocuments, abandoning and closing a portion of a Utility Easement, and related documents, located in\nLot 1, O.L. Slaton School Addition within Section 9, Block B, Lubbock County, between Avenue P\nand Avenue Q, north of 32nd Street.\n\n6. 4.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Right-of-Way: Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0063, and related\ndocuments, abandoning and closing a portion of an alley located between Tract 1D2, Snow Davis\nAddition, and Lot 1, McGuire Addition, located in Section 44, Block AK, Lubbock County, south of\n19th Street and west of Frankford Avenue.\n \n6. 5.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Right-of-Way: Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0064, and related\ndocuments, abandoning and closing a portion of a Right-of-Way adjacent to Elgin Avenue, located in\nSection 1, Block AK, of Lubbock County Texas, along Elgin Avenue between 133rd Street and 136th\nStreet.\n \n6. 6.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Right-of-Way: Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0065, and related\ndocuments, abandoning and closing a 2.165-acre portion of the Gates of Glory, an Addition to the City\nof Lubbock, located in Section 18, Block E-2, on the east side of Memphis Avenue, south of 111th\nStreet, and north of 113th Street.\n \n6. 7.\nOrdinance 1st Reading - Right-of-Way: Consider an ordinance, and related documents, abandoning\nand closing a portion of right-of-way adjacent to Utica Avenue at 142nd Street, located in Section 5,\nBlock AK, Lubbock County. \n \n6. 8.\nResolution - Right-of-Way: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute a Memorandum of\nAgreement, with Alfred Arthur Brockopp, Jr., Kimberli Ann Austin a/k/a Kimberly Ann Austin,\nTiffany Kay Austin a/k/a Tiffany Kay Austin Shannon, Judy Alsup a/k/a Judy Gail Price Alsup, Sherry\nPatton Brady a/k/a Sherry Lasha Brady, Patty Kay Patton Wright a/k/a Patti Kay Wright, Carolyn Sue\nPrice Thornton a/k/a Carolyn Sue Thornton and Delia Renee O’Donnell, for the purchase of a\n0.093-acre tract of land located in the southeast quarter (SE ¼) of Section 34, Block AK, Georgetown\nRailroad Co. Survey, Abstract No. 1385, Lubbock County, Texas (Parcel A), located on the west side\nof Upland Avenue, between 61st Street and 63rd Street, to be utilized for the 2022 Street Bond Project. \n \n6. 9.\nResolution - Right-of-Way: Consider a resolution rejecting any and all bids received for the purchase\nof City-owned real property, a 3.27-acre tract of land in Section 22, Block AK, Lubbock County,\nTexas, per ITB 26-19577-SR. \n \n6. 10.\nResolution - Right-of-Way: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute Contract 19547,\nand related documents, by and between the City of Lubbock and Assembly Construction, Inc., for the\nsale of real property, a 0.7014-acre tract out of Section 16, Block A, Abstract 820, Lubbock County,\nTexas, at 1207 North Avenue T. \n \n6. 11.\nResolution - Engineering: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute Amendment No. 1\nto Contract 18588, and related documents, with Freese and Nichols, Inc., for construction phase\nservices, related to the reconstruction of Broadway, from Avenue Q to Avenue E, to be utilized for the\n2024 Street Bond Project. \n \n6. 12.\nResolution - Engineering: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute Construction\nServices Contract 19633, with Ti -Zack Concrete, LLC, for Broadway reconstruction, as a portion of\nthe 2024 Street Bond Project.\n\n6. 13.\nResolution - Engineering: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute Public Works\nContract 19431, by and between the City of Lubbock and MH Civil Constructors, Inc., for the West\nLubbock Water System Expansion. \n \n6. 14.\nOrdinance 1st Reading - Public Works, Traffic Management: Consider an ordinance amending\nSection 20.05.103 of the City of Lubbock Code of Ordinances, with regard to the establishment of\nschool zones and speed limits, on Norfolk Avenue between 130th Street and 136th Street, and on 135th\nStreet between Quaker Avenue and Memphis Avenue. \n \n6. 15.\nResolution - Public Works, Paved Streets: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute\nContract 19530, with Lone Star Dirt & Paving, Ltd., for the Dunbar/Manhattan Heights Rebuild\nof portions of Redbud Avenue, north of the intersection of East 24th Street to the dead end, and Teak\nAvenue from Redbud Avenue to East 31st Street, to be utilized for the 2022 Street Bond Project. \n \n6. 16.\nResolution - Business Development: Consider a resolution approving the method of assessment\nclassification for the Centerpointe Public Improvement District, and calling for a Public Hearing on\nJuly 14, 2026. \n \n6. 17.\nResolution - Business Development: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute\nContract 19455, and related documents, with Turfmaster Irrigation and Landscaping, Inc., for North\nOverton Tax Increment Finance Districts Irrigation Improvements. \n \n6. 18.\nResolution - Business Development: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute Contract\n19643, and related documents, with West Texas Services dba Tom’s Tree Place for North Overton\nPublic Improvement District Landscape Maintenance and Bird Mitigation. \n \n6. 19.\nResolution - Business Development: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute\nAmendment No. 2 to Professional Services Agreement, Contract 19005, with West Texas Services,\nInc., dba Tom's Tree Place, for services related to landscaping in the medians at Glenna Goodacre\nBoulevard in the North Overton Tax Increment Finance District boundary, following the closure of 3\nintersections. \n \n6. 20.\nResolution - Business Development: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute Change\nOrder No. 1 for Contract 18607, with MH Civil Constructors, Inc., for hardscape repairs, including\nsidewalks, concrete paving, brick pavers, curbs, and other pedestrian-oriented infrastructure located\nwithin the public right-of-way, in the North Overton Tax Increment Finance District. \n \n6. 21.\nResolution - Fleet Services: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute Contract 19380\nwith Bruckner’s Truck & Equipment, Contract 19527 with Lubbock Truck Sales, Contract 19528 with\nAmerican Equipment & Trailer, Contract 19529 with Longley Diesel and Equipment Service, Contract\n19531 with Cummins Southern Plains, Contract 19532 with Associated Supply Company, and Contract\n19533 with Rush Truck Center of Texas, for heavy-duty maintenance and repairs for City vehicles and\nequipment. \n\n6. 22.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Planning (District 2): Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0067, for Zone\nCase 2565-I, a request of Hugo Reed & Associates for CRS Business Park, LLC, for a zone change\nfrom Heavy Commercial District (HC) and Industrial Park District (IP) to Heavy Commercial District\n(HC), at 101 66th Street, 103 66th Street, 107 66th Street, 6660 Ash Avenue, 6662 Ash Avenue, 7002\nAsh Avenue, 7008 Ash Avenue, and 7010 Ash Avenue. Generally located south of 66th Street and\nwest of Ash Avenue, Crossroads South Business Park Addition, Tracts A, D, E, F, G, I, J, and K.\n \n6. 23.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Planning (District 5): Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0068, for Zone Case\n3546, a request of McDougal Realtors for Premier Apex, LLC, for a zone change from Low Density\nSingle-Family District (SF-2) to General Industrial District (GI), at 7806 76th Street, located east of\nAlcove Avenue and north of Marsha Sharp Freeway, on 10.001 acres of unplatted land out of Block\nAK, Section 31.\n \n6. 24.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Planning (District 6): Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0070, for Zone Case\n3547, a request of Parkhill for St. John Neumann Catholic Diocese, for a zone change from Low\nDensity Single-Family District (SF-2) to Heavy Commercial District (HC), generally located east of\nWest Loop 289 and north of 22nd Street, on 2.08 acres of land out of McGuire Addition, Lot 1.\n \n6. 25.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Planning (District 6): Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0069, for Zone Case\n3545, a request for zone changes in City Council District 6 from Low Density Single-Family District\n(SF-2), Medium Density Residential District (MDR), High Density Residential District (HDR),\nNeighborhood Commercial District (NC), Auto-Urban Commercial District (AC), Heavy Commercial\nDistrict (HC), Industrial Park District (IP) and Light Industrial District (LI) to Low Density\nSingle-Family District (SF-2), Medium Density Residential District (MDR), High Density Residential\nDistrict (HDR), Neighborhood Commercial District (NC), Auto-Urban Commercial District (AC),\nHeavy Commercial District (HC), and Light Industrial District (LI), at 6007, 6015, and 6023 45th\nStreet, Lots 3-A-1, 3-A-1-A, and 3-A-2, Santa Fe Park Addition, 6025 45th Street, 3.7 acres of\nunplatted land out of Block AK, Section 37, 6027 45th Street, Tract A, Isom Pearl Addition, 6029,\n6033, 6039, 6107, 6109, and 6113 45th Street, Lots 9, 12, 13, 22, and 23, Santa Fe Park Addition, 309\nNorth Slide Road, 5.66 acres out of Tract K-2, North Park Addition, 5006 Auburn Street, Tract C-1,\nNorth Park Addition, 4809, 4811, and 4815 Emory Street, Tracts F-1, F-2, and F-3, Physicians\nSurgicenter Lubbock Addition, 4810 North Loop 289, 6.1 acres out of Tract B, Physicians Surgicenter\nLubbock Addition, 415 and 421 North Utica Avenue, Tracts D and E, Physicians Surgicenter Lubbock\nAddition, 4802 North Loop 289, 0.19 acres out of Tract C, Physicians Surgicenter Lubbock Addition,\n418 and 424 North Utica Avenue, Tract DD-1-A and DD-1-B, Physicians Surgicenter Lubbock\nAddition, 410 North Utica Avenue, 0.6 acres out of Tract EE-1, Physicians Surgicenter Lubbock\nAddition, 4640, 4642, and 4650 North Loop 289, Tract A, Physicians Surgicenter Lubbock Addition,\n430 North Utica Drive, Tract DD-1-C, Physicians Surgicenter Lubbock Addition, 4641 Erskine Street,\nTract H, DD-1-B, Physicians Surgicenter Lubbock Addition, 5710 4th Street, 1.16 acres out of Tract E,\nWest Wind Addition, 5212 4th Street, Tract C-1-A-2, Whisperwood Addition, 5402 4th Street, the\nn