2.01 acres of\nunplatted land out of Block JS, Section 12, 3303 North Frankford Avenue, 5.02 acres of unplatted land\nout of Block JS, Section 12, 3105 North Frankford Avenue, 4.36 acres of unplatted land out of Block\nJS, Section 12, 2905 North Frankford Avenue, 5.02 acres of unplatted land out of Block JS, Section\n12, 2607 North Frankford Avenue, 5.02 acres of unplatted land out of Block JS, Section 12, 2910\nNorth Frankford Avenue, 6.15 acres of unplatted land out of Block JS, Section 11, 2902 North\nFrankford Avenue, 6 acres of unplatted land out of Block JS, Section 11, 2612 North Frankford\nAvenue, 1 acre of unplatted land out of Block JS, Section 11, 2317 North Frankford Avenue, 5.01\nacres of unplatted land out of Block JS, Section 12, 2309 North Frankford Avenue, 2.58 acres of\nunplatted land out of Block JS, Section 12, 2703 North Quaker Avenue, Tract A, Stauffer Chemical\nAddition, 2715 North Quaker Avenue, 7.98 acres of unplatted land out of Block A, Section 14, 4501\nBradley Street, the east 401.09 feet of Lot A, T C I Addition, 2213 North Quaker Avenue, 1.49 acres of\nunplatted land out of Block A, Section 14, 4401 Clovis Road, 2.59 acres of unplatted land out of Block\nA, Section 14, 4403 Clovis Road, Tract A, Rollins Addition, 4405 Clovis Road, Tract A, Saunders\nAddition, 4407 Clovis Road, 1.55 acres of unplatted land out of Block A, Section 14, 4409 Clovis\nRoad, 2 acres of unplatted land out of Block A, Section 14, and 4413 Clovis Road, 2.60 acres of\nunplatted land out of Block A, Section 14.\n \n7.\nRegular Agenda\n \n7. 1.\nBoard Appointments - City Secretary: Consider appointments of City Council members to the South\nPlains Association of Governments (SPAG) Board. \n \n7. 2.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Engineering: Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0052, amending Chapter 36\nof the Code of Ordinances by adding “Division 2 Paving Alleys by Petition” to Article 36.08,\nestablishing a process for the paving of unimproved alleys through a petition-initiated assessment\nprocess, and providing for placing a lien on property for unpaid assessments."}, {"title": "2026-06-08 - June 2026 Library Board Meeting (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06082026-89", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "City of Lubbock, Texas Library Board Meeting June 15th, at 12:00 PM Mahon Community Room 1306 9th St, Lubbock, TX 79407 1) Call to Order Welcome and introductions – Patricia Maloney 2) Minutes Consider the approval of the May 18th, 2026 meeting minutes. 3) Citizen Comments According to City of Lubbock Board Rules, any citizen wishing to appear before a regular meeting of the Libra", "text": "City of Lubbock, Texas \nLibrary Board Meeting \nJune 15th, at 12:00 PM \nMahon Community Room \n1306 9th St, Lubbock, TX 79407 \n \n1) Call to Order \nWelcome and introductions – Patricia Maloney \n \n2) Minutes \nConsider the approval of the May 18th, 2026 meeting minutes. \n \n3) Citizen Comments \nAccording to City of Lubbock Board Rules, any citizen wishing to appear before a regular meeting of the \nLibrary Board, regarding any matter posted on the Library Board Agenda below, shall complete the sign-up \nform provided at the meeting, no later than 12:00 p.m. Any citizen wishing to comment on any matter posted on \nthe Library Board agenda below that will not be in attendance in person may submit a citizen comment by email \nat HStewart@mylubbock.us, no later than 8:00 a.m. on the date of the meeting. Submitted comments must \ninclude name and address. Each comment will be read aloud for a period of time not to exceed three minutes \npursuant to City of Lubbock Board Rules. Citizen Comments is an opportunity for citizens to make comments \nand express a position on agenda items. Any comment received that is in the nature of asking a question will be \nreferred to an appropriate member of the library or City staff for a response and will not be read aloud at the \nmeeting. In accordance with the Texas Open Meetings Act, the Libraries Board may not take action on public \nmatters during Citizen Comments. \n \n4) Presentations \n 4.1) Meet the Staff-Patterson Branch Library \n 4.2) Lubbock Library Director Report – Hannah Stewart, Lubbock Library Director \n 4.3) FOL President Report – Lynne Strickland, FOL Chair \n 4.4) Genealogical Society Report- Kathy Kitten \n\n5) Work Session \n 5.1) Discussion – A discussion pertaining to housekeeping items and future meeting agenda items. \n \n 5.2) Next regularly scheduled meeting will be at noon on August 17th, 2026 at the Mahon Library. There is no \nboard meeting in July. \n\nLubbock Libraries Board meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special assistance, please contact the City of \nLubbock at 806-775-2826 or write to 1306 9th Street, Lubbock, TX 79401 at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting."}, {"title": "2026-06-04 - Transportation Advisory Committee (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06042026-79", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "Transportation Advisory Committee June 4th, 2026, 10:00 a.m. 916 Main Street, 2nd Floor Conference Room Lubbock, Texas 79401 1. Call to Order of the Transportation Advisory Committee 2. Acknowledgment of Quorum 3. Safety Procedures 4. Public Comment and Acknowledgment of Guests Members of the public may comment on items listed on the agenda. Comments are limited to three minut", "text": "Transportation Advisory Committee \nJune 4th, 2026, 10:00 a.m. \n916 Main Street, 2nd Floor Conference Room \nLubbock, Texas 79401 \n \n1. \nCall to Order of the Transportation Advisory Committee \n \n2. \nAcknowledgment of Quorum \n \n3. \nSafety Procedures \n \n4. \nPublic Comment and Acknowledgment of Guests \nMembers of the public may comment on items listed on the agenda. Comments are \nlimited to three minutes per speaker. \n \n5. \nConsider approval of the May 12th, 2026, meeting minutes for the Transportation \nAdvisory Committee. \n \n6. \nUnified Planning Work Program (UPWP) 2025 – 2026 Update \n \nDiscussion and Recommendation: \n \nStaff will provide an update on the amendment to the FY 2025–2026 UPWP, with context on \nthe direction received from the Transportation Policy Committee. \nAction Requested: No action \n \n7. \nUnified Planning Work Program (UPWP) 2027 – 2028 Update \n \nDiscussion and Recommendation: \n \nStaff will provide an update on the development of the FY 2027–2028 UPWP, including \ncoordination status, task structure, schedule milestones, and anticipated timelines for draft \ndevelopment and committee review. \nAction Requested: Discussion, report findings to the Transportation Policy Committee. \n \n8. \nLocal Funding Mechanism \n\nDiscussion and Recommendation: \n \nStaff will provide a case study review of how other governmental agencies have pulled \ntogether funds for grant funding set aside \n \nAction Requested: Discussion, report findings to the Transportation Policy Committee. \n \n9. \nReports: \n• \nTxDOT \n• \nCitibus \n1. Update regarding 10CR Fund Transfer \n• \nLPD/DPS \n• \nTexas Tech University \n• \nLMPO’s \n1. MPO, Fiscal Agent, and TxDOT Contract \n2. Lubbock County Contract (space leasing) \n3. LMPO Boundary Expansion \n4. Grant Pursuits \n5. 10-Yr Plan \n6. Acronym and Document Map \n \n11. \nAdjournment \n\nComité Asesor de Transporte \nJunio 4, 2026, 10:00 a.m. \n916 Main Street, 2ª planta Sala de conferencias \nLubbock, Texas 79401 \n \n1. \nConvocatoria al Orden del Comité Asesor de Transporte \n \n2. \nReconocimiento del Quórum \n \n3. \nProcedimientos de seguridad \n \n4. \nComentarios y agradecimientos públicos a los invitados \nEl público puede comentar los puntos listados en la agenda. Los comentarios están \nlimitados a tres minutos por ponente. \n \n5. \nConsidere la aprobación del acta de la reunión del 12 de mayo de 2026 para el Comité \nAsesor de Transporte. \n \n6. \nPrograma de Trabajo de Planificación Unificada (UPWP) Actualización 2025 – 2026 \n \nDebate y recomendaciones: \n \nEl personal proporcionará una actualización sobre la enmienda al UPWP del año fiscal 2025–\n2026, con contexto sobre las directrices recibidas del Comité de Política de Transporte. \nAcción solicitada: Sin acción \n \n7. \nPrograma de Trabajo de Planificación Unificada (UPWP) Actualización 2027 – 2028 \n \nDebate y recomendaciones: \n \nEl personal proporcionará una actualización sobre el desarrollo del UPWP del año fiscal \n2027–2028, incluyendo el estado de coordinación, la estructura de la tarea, los hitos del \ncalendario y los plazos previstos para el desarrollo del borrador y la revisión del comité. \nSe solicita acción: Discusión, informe de las conclusiones al Comité de Política de \nTransporte. \n\n8. \nMecanismo de financiación local \n \nDebate y recomendaciones: \n \nEl personal proporcionará una revisión de caso sobre cómo otras agencias \ngubernamentales han reunido fondos para la financiación de subvenciones reservadas \n \nSe solicita acción: Discusión, informe de las conclusiones al Comité de Política de \nTransporte. \n \n9. \nInformes: \n• \nTxDOT \n• \nCitibus \n1. Actualización sobre la transferencia del fondo 10CR \n• \nLPD/DPS \n• \nUniversidad Tecnológica de Texas \n• \nLMPO's \n1. MPO, Agente Fiscal y Contrato TxDOT \n2. Contrato del condado de Lubbock (arrendamiento de espacio) \n3. Expansión de límites de la LMPO \n4. Actividades de la subvención \n5. Plan a 10 años \n6. Acrónimo y mapa de documentos \n \n11. \nSuspensión de la sesión"}, {"title": "2026-06-02 - Appointments Advisory Board - 11:30 AM (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_06022026-75", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "Brett Underwood, Chair Bruce Boyd, Vice Chair Cathy Allen, District 6 Rep. Colton Davis, District 3 Rep. Monica Delgado, District 2 Rep. Rafael Gutierrez, District 1 Rep. Ryan Henry, District 6 Rep. Heather Keister, Mayor Rep. Margaret Kelley, District 5 Rep. Appointments Advisory Board Agenda June 2, 2026 11:30 A.M. Citizens Tower 2nd Floor Conference Rooms 201A/B 1314 Ave. K", "text": "Brett Underwood, Chair \nBruce Boyd, Vice Chair \nCathy Allen, District 6 Rep. \nColton Davis, District 3 Rep. \nMonica Delgado, District 2 Rep. \nRafael Gutierrez, District 1 Rep. \nRyan Henry, District 6 Rep. \nHeather Keister, Mayor Rep. \nMargaret Kelley, District 5 Rep. \n\nAppointments Advisory Board \nAgenda \n June 2, 2026 \n 11:30 A.M. \n \nCitizens Tower \n2nd Floor Conference Rooms 201A/B \n1314 Ave. K , Lubbock, Texas \n\n Margarita Olivarez, District 1 Rep. \n Andrea Parker, District 2 Rep. \n Keith Patrick, Mayor Rep. \n Tiffany Robinson, District 3 Rep. \n Amy Sikes, District 4 Rep. \n Tyler Young, District 5 Rep. \n Courtney Paz, City Secretary \n Jimmy Maynard, Deputy City Secretary \n\nAppointments Advisory Board meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special assistance, please \ncontact the Office of the City Secretary at 806.775.2026, e-mail ocs@mylubbock.us, or write to Post Office Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas \n79457 at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting. \n \nPursuant to the City Council’s policy on Boards, Commissions, and Committees, one or more members of the Appointments Advisory \nBoard may participate in the meeting by video-conference call as permitted under Section XVIII of the policy. \n \n1. \nCall to order \n \n2. \nReflections \n \n3. Minutes \n \n3.1 \nMay 5, 2026 Regular Appointments Advisory Board Meeting \n \n4. \nRegular Session \n \n4.1 \nAudit & Investment Committee – Consider recommendations for appointments \n \n4.2 Appointments Advisory Board – Consider recommendations for appointments \n \n4.3 Building Board of Appeals – Consider recommendations for appointments \n \n4.4 StarCare Board of Trustees – Consider recommendations for appointments \n \n4.5 \nDiscussion and Action if necessary on the Following Boards from the April 7, 2026 and May 5, \n2026 Meetings – Canadian River Municipal Water Authority Board of Directors, Citizens Traffic \nCommission, Civic Lubbock, Inc. Board of Directors, Lubbock Water Advisory Commission, and the \nPermit & License Appeal Board \n \n5. \nWork Session \n \n 5.1 \nDiscuss and consider recruiting and participation methods for boards and commissions service \n \n 5.2 \nDiscussion – A discussion pertaining to boards and commissions policies and procedures, \nrecommendation process for prospective board members, board applicants, housekeeping items \n(including board packets), directives to the staff liaison and future meeting agenda items."}, {"title": "2026-05-28 - Veterans Advisory Committee - 12:00 PM (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_05282026-74", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "Veterans Advisory Committee Agenda May 28th, 2026 12:00 p.m. Citizens Tower, 2nd Floor Conference Center Rooms 201A & 201B 1314 Avenue K Lubbock, TX 79401 (1) Call to Order (2) Citizen Comments - According to HB 2840, any citizen wishing to appear before a regular meeting of Veterans Advisory Committee, regarding any matter posted on the Veterans Advisory Committee Agenda, shall", "text": "Veterans Advisory Committee \nAgenda \nMay 28th, 2026 \n12:00 p.m. \n \nCitizens Tower, 2nd Floor Conference Center \nRooms 201A & 201B \n1314 Avenue K \nLubbock, TX 79401 \n \n(1) \nCall to Order \n \n(2) \nCitizen Comments - According to HB 2840, any citizen wishing to appear before a regular \nmeeting of Veterans Advisory Committee, regarding any matter posted on the Veterans \nAdvisory Committee Agenda, shall complete the sign-up form provided at the meeting, no \nlater than 12:00 p.m. \n \n(3) \nMinutes: Consider and act on the approval of the minutes from the April 23, 2026 Veterans \nAdvisory Committee meeting. \n \n(4) \nReview new Veterans Advisory Committee Logos and take appropriate action as needed \n \n(5) \nDiscuss new Veteran Needs Assessment and take appropriate action as needed \n \n(6) \nDiscuss West Texas Salute to Veterans and take appropriate action as needed \n \n(7) \nUpdate on the West Texas State Veterans Cemetery \n \n(8) \nUpdate from the Veterans Advisory Committee Mission and Vision Sub-Committee and \ntake appropriate action as needed \n \n(9) \nUpdate from the Purple Heart Coin Sub-Committee and take appropriate action as needed \n \n(10) Presentation from Veteran Housing Sub-Committee (3-5 minutes) \n \n(11) Presentation from Veteran Mental Health Sub-Committee (3-5 minutes) \n \n(12) Presentation from Veteran’s Court Sub-Committee (3-5 minutes) \n \n(13) Presentation from Women Veterans Sub-Committee (3-5 minutes) \n \n(14) Adjourn \nDate of next scheduled meeting: June 25th, 2026"}, {"title": "2026-05-28 - Public Transit Advisory Board - 11:30 AM (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_05282026-73", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "NOTICE OF LUBBOCK PUBLIC TRANSIT ADVISORY BOARD MEETING MAY 28, 2026 – 11:30 A.M. CITIBUS CONFERENCE ROOM, 801 TEXAS LUBBOCK, TEXAS 1. Call to Order 2. Citizen Comments - According to HB 2840, any citizen wishing to appear before a regular meeting of the Public Transit Advisory Board, regarding any matter posted on the Public Transit Advisory Board Agenda, shall sign-up no later than 11", "text": "NOTICE OF LUBBOCK PUBLIC TRANSIT ADVISORY BOARD MEETING \nMAY 28, 2026 – 11:30 A.M. \nCITIBUS CONFERENCE ROOM, 801 TEXAS \nLUBBOCK, TEXAS \n \n1. Call to Order \n \n2. Citizen Comments - According to HB 2840, any citizen wishing to appear before a regular meeting \nof the Public Transit Advisory Board, regarding any matter posted on the Public Transit Advisory \nBoard Agenda, shall sign-up no later than 11:15 a.m. on the day of the meeting by the following \nmethods: \n2.1.1. E-mail sgarrett@citibus.com; \n2.1.2. Call Citibus at 806-775-3640; or \n2.1.3. In person at 801 Texas Avenue \n \n3. Ceremonial Items \n \n3.1. Employee Recognition \n \n3.2. Recognition of Outgoing Board Member \n \n4. Minutes \n\n4.1. Consider approval of the minutes of the March 27, 2026, regular meeting of the Lubbock \nPublic Transit Advisory Board (TAB) \n \n5. Regular Session/Action Items \n \n5.1. Acceptance of Citibus Financial and Operating Reports \n \n5.2. Consider approval of the Public Transit Agency Safety Plan Addendum 1 as Directed in the \nBipartisan Infrastructure Law (BIL) \n \n5.3. Consider Approval of Updated Fleet Replacement Plan \n \n5.4. Discussion and Election of Chairperson and Vice Chairperson \n \n5.5. Consider Recommendation of Items to be Presented to City Council for Approval \n5.5.1 Consider recommendation of contract with Western Collision for body work and \naccident damage repair for Citibus vehicles. \n \n6. Work Session \n \n6.1. Update on Citibus Marketing \n \n6.2. Update on Citibus Operations \n \n6.3. Update on Citibus Maintenance Operations \n\n6.4. General Manager Update \n \n7. Adjourn \n \nNOTICE OF MEETING was posted outside the South entrance \nof Citizens Tower, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas, on the 21st \nday of May 2026 at ______P.M. \n \nBy: ______________________________________ \n Shannon Garrett, Board Support Staff Member \n \nThe Lubbock Public Transit Advisory Board meetings are available to all persons regardless of \ndisability. If you require special assistance, please contact Shannon Garrett at (806) 775-3434, or \nwrite to her at P.O. Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas 79457, at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting."}, {"title": "2026-05-27 - Model Codes and construction Advisory Board-3:30PM *Canceled* (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_05272026-67", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "Current Board Members Gary Ferguson, Chair James Jordan, Vice Chair Kendall Wood, Master Electrician Ryan Farquhar, Commercial Contractor David Small, Engineer Logan West, Facilities Manager Craig Ray, WTHBA Brian Robertson, Engineer Wendell Burris, Lubbock Apartment Marvin White, Licensed HVAC George Henson, Licensed Plumber Jacob Cline, Electrician Model Codes and Construction Adv", "text": "Current Board Members \n \nGary Ferguson, Chair \nJames Jordan, Vice Chair \nKendall Wood, Master Electrician \nRyan Farquhar, Commercial Contractor \nDavid Small, Engineer \nLogan West, Facilities Manager \nCraig Ray, WTHBA \nBrian Robertson, Engineer \nWendell Burris, Lubbock Apartment \nMarvin White, Licensed HVAC \nGeorge Henson, Licensed Plumber \nJacob Cline, Electrician \nModel Codes and Construction Advisory - Meeting Agenda \nMay 27, 2026, 3:30 P.M. \nCitizens Tower \n1st Floor Council Chambers Workroom \n1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas \nModel Codes and Construction Advisory Board meetings are available to all \npeople regardless of disability. If you require special assistance, please contact \nthe Building Safety Department at 806.775.3191, e-mail \nmvillagrana@mylubbock.us, or write to Post Office Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas \n79457 at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting. \n \nCall to Order for Regular Meeting \n1. \nApproval of Minutes \na. \nApril 22, 2026, Regular meeting \nAction Items \n2. \nThe Board will discuss and take appropriate action on the following items: \nDates at the end of each code set are proposed for presentations (may ﬂuctuate) \n \na. \n 2021/2024 International Existing Building Code – Completed -July 2025 \n \nb. \n2021/2024 International Building Code-Completed- January 2026 \nc. \n2021/2024 International Fire Code – Partial Completion -January 2026 \nd. \n2021/2024 International Fuel Gas Code – Completed-March 2026 \ne. \n2021/2024 International Swimming Pool and Spa Code – May 2026 \nf. \n2021/2024 International Plumbing Code- May 2026 \ng. \n2021/2024 International Mechanical Code – May 2026 \nh. \n2021/2024 International Residential Code- June 2026 \n\ni. \n2020/2023/2026 National Electric Code – July 2026 \nj. \n2021/2024 International Energy Conservation Code –July 2026 \n \nNext meeting is scheduled for June 24, 2026."}, {"title": "2026-05-27 - Meet and Confer Negotiations - Police - 3:00 PM (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_05272026-50", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "Notice of Open Deliberations Pursuant to Tex. Loc. Gov’t Code § 142.063, this public notice is provided relating to meet and confer deliberations between: City of Lubbock, Texas and Lubbock Professional Police Association Date/Time: May 27, 2026 at 3:00 P.M. Location: Citizens Tower, 2nd Floor Conference Center, 201A/B, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas 79401 Agenda: Deliberations and/or", "text": "Notice of Open Deliberations \nPursuant to Tex. Loc. Gov’t Code § 142.063, this public notice is provided relating to meet and confer \ndeliberations between: \nCity of Lubbock, Texas \nand \nLubbock Professional Police Association \n \nDate/Time: \nMay 27, 2026 at 3:00 P.M. \nLocation: \nCitizens Tower, 2nd Floor Conference Center, 201A/B, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas \n79401 \nAgenda: \nDeliberations and/or related action relating to an agreement or a proposed agreement \nbetween the City of Lubbock, Texas (“City”) and the Lubbock Professional Police \nAssociation (“Association”) as provided for in Texas Local Government Code Chapter \n142, Subchapter B. \nPublic Notice: \nMembers of the public and press are encouraged to observe and monitor the deliberation. A recording of \nthe public portion of the meeting will be made available, but active participation in discussions or \npresentations is expressly prohibited unless permitted by the Ground Rules established by the City and the \nAssociation. \nRepresentatives for either the City or Association may suspend the meeting at any time during the \nproceedings for consultation with their attorney or to have a private caucus with their respective \nrepresentatives. Pursuant to Section 551.071 of the Texas Government Code and Section 142.063(b) of the \nTexas Local Government Code the deliberations during this period are closed to the public \nThe use of cellular phones or sound activated pagers is prohibited while deliberations are being conducted. \nPlease step outside the meeting room should you elect to utilize these devices. \nThis meeting is available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special assistance, please \ncontact the City Secretary's Office at (806)775-2061 or write to Post Office Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas \n79457 at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting."}, {"title": "2026-05-26 - Regular City Council Meeting, May 26, 2026 (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_05262026-71", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "City of Lubbock, Texas Regular City Council Meeting May 26, 2026 Mark W. McBrayer, Mayor Christy Martinez-Garcia, Mayor Pro Tem, District 1 Gordon Harris, Councilman, District 2 David Bruegel, Councilman, District 3 Brayden Rose, Councilman, District 4 Dr. Jennifer Wilson, Councilwoman, District 5 Tim Collins, Councilman, District 6 W. Jarrett Atkinson, City Manager Matt Wade, City Attorney Cour", "text": "City of Lubbock, Texas\nRegular City Council Meeting\nMay 26, 2026\nMark W. McBrayer, Mayor\nChristy Martinez-Garcia, Mayor Pro Tem, District 1\nGordon Harris, Councilman, District 2\nDavid Bruegel, Councilman, District 3\nBrayden Rose, Councilman, District 4\nDr. Jennifer Wilson, Councilwoman, District 5\nTim Collins, Councilman, District 6\n \nW. Jarrett Atkinson, City Manager\nMatt Wade, City Attorney\nCourtney Paz, City Secretary\nhttp://www.mylubbock.us\nCity Council Chambers, Citizens Tower, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas\n \nCity of Lubbock City Council Meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special assistance, please contact\nthe City Secretary's Office at (806)775-2061 or write to Post Office Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas 79457 at least 48 hours in advance of the\nmeeting. \nExecutive Session Disclosure Statement: The City Council reserves the right to adjourn into executive session at any time during the course of\nthe meeting to discuss any item listed on this agenda as authorized by Chapter 551 of the Texas Government Code, including but not\nnecessarily limited to §551.071 (Consultation with Attorney), §551.072 (Deliberations regarding Real Property), §551.073 (Deliberations\nregarding Gifts and Donations), §551.074 (Personnel Matters), §551.076 (Deliberations regarding Security Devices), §551.086 (Public\nPower Utilities: Competitive Matters), §551.087 (Deliberations regarding Economic Development Negotiations). \nA quorum of the City Council will be physically present in City Council Chambers located in Citizens Tower, 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas,\nas it is the intent of the City Council to have a quorum physically present at this location. One or more members of the City Council, however,\nmay participate in the meeting by video-conference call as permitted under Section 551.127 of the Texas Government Code. \nNote: On occasion, the City Council may consider agenda items out of order. \n. \n \n12:00 p.m. - City Council convenes in City Council Chambers and immediately recesses into Executive\nSession.\n\n1.\nExecutive Session\n \n1. 1.\nHold an executive session in accordance with Texas Government Code, Section 551.071, with legal\ncounsel for advice about pending or contemplated litigation or settlement agreement and on matters in\nwhich the duty of the attorney under the Texas Disciplinary Rules of Professional Conduct conflicts\nwith Chapter 551. \n \n1. 1. 1.\nQuaker Avenue Development Agreement; Contract No. 17488; Code of Ordinances Chapter 41\nTexas Local Government Code Chapter 395, Impact Fees - Notice of Claim\n \n1. 2.\nHold an executive session in accordance with Texas Government Code, Section 551.087, to discuss or\ndeliberate regarding commercial or financial information that the governmental body has received from\na business prospect that the governmental body seeks to have locate, stay, or expand in or near the\nterritory of the governmental body and with which the governmental body is conducting economic\ndevelopment negotiations; and to deliberate the offer of a financial or other incentive to a business\nprospect described herein above. \n\n1. 2. 1.\nProject Playa\n \nAdjourn from Executive Session\n \n2:00 p.m. - City Council reconvenes in Open Session in City Council Chambers.\n \n2.\nCeremonial Items\n \n2. 1.\nInvocation \n \n2. 2.\nPledges of Allegiance \n \nCall to Order\n \n3.\nCitizen Comments - According to Lubbock City Council Rules, any citizen wishing to appear\nin-person before a regular meeting of the City Council, regarding any matter posted on the City\nCouncil Agenda below, shall complete the sign-up form provided at the meeting, no later than\n2:00 p.m. on May 26, 2026. Citizen Comments provide an opportunity for citizens to make\ncomments and express a position on agenda items. \n \n4.\nMinutes\n \n4. 1.\nApril 28, 2026 Regular City Council Meeting \n \n5.\nConsent Agenda - Items considered to be routine are enacted by one motion without separate\ndiscussion. If the City Council desires to discuss an item, the item is removed from the Consent\nAgenda and considered separately.\n \n5. 1.\nBudget Ordinance Amendment 2nd Reading - Finance: Consider Budget Ordinance No.\n2026-O0057, Amendment 27, respecting the General Fund in connection with Cost Center 4211, Code\nEnforcement Operating Budget - Demolitions. \n \n5. 2.\nBudget Ordinance Amendment 2nd Reading - Finance: Consider Budget Ordinance No.\n2026-O0053, Amendment 28, respecting the North Point Public Improvement District Fund, for\nadditional funding for public improvements related to Contract 18386.\n \n5. 3.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Finance: Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0054, amending Ordinance No.\n2025-O0108, Exhibit “B”, the 2025 Service and Assessment Plan for the North Point Public\nImprovement District, by including additional funding for public improvements for Contract 18386. \n\n5. 4.\nBudget Ordinance Amendment 1st Reading - Finance: Consider an ordinance amending Section IV\nof Budget Amendment 18, to the FY 2025-26 Budget for municipal purposes, respecting the transfer\nfrom the Airport Operating Fund to the Airport Capital Project Fund, correcting a clerical error. \n \n5. 5.\nResolution - Risk Management: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute Professional\nServices Agreement, Contract 19575, with USI Insurance Services, LLC and Alera Group, for\nconsulting and broker services for property and casualty insurance.\n \n5. 6.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Right-of-Way: Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0055, abandoning and\nclosing a portion of a drainage easement located in Tracts A, H, I, and J of the Legacy Range Business\nPark Addition, within Section 21, Block E-2, Lubbock County, Texas, on the south side of 116th\nStreet, east of Indiana Avenue. \n \n5. 7.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Right-of-Way: Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0056, abandoning and\nclosing a portion of drainage easements located to the east of the intersection of 88th Street and Urbana\nAvenue, within Section 26, Block AK, Lubbock County, Texas, located west of Upland Avenue, and\neast of Urbana Avenue, at 88th Street and 90th Street.\n \n5. 8.\nOrdinance 1st Reading - Right-of-Way: Consider an ordinance, and related documents, abandoning\nand closing a portion of an alley located between Tract 1D2, Snow Davis Addition, and Lot 1,\nMcGuire Addition, located in Section 44, Block AK, Lubbock County, south of 19th Street and west of\nFrankford Avenue.\n \n5. 9.\nOrdinance 1st Reading - Right-of-Way: Consider an ordinance, and related documents, abandoning\nand closing a portion of a Right-of-Way adjacent to Elgin Avenue, located in Section 1, Block AK, of\nLubbock County Texas, along Elgin Avenue between 133rd Street and 136th Street.\n \n5. 10.\nOrdinance 1st Reading - Right-of-Way: Consider an ordinance, and related documents, abandoning\nand closing a 2.165-acre portion of the Gates of Glory, an Addition to the City of Lubbock, located in\nSection 18, Block E-2, on the east side of Memphis Avenue, south of 111th Street, and north of 113th\nStreet.\n \n5. 11.\nOrdinance 1st Reading - Right-of-Way: Consider an ordinance, and related documents, abandoning\nand closing a portion of a Utility Easement, and related documents, located in Lot 1, O.L. Slaton\nSchool Addition within Section 9, Block B, Lubbock County, between Avenue P and Avenue Q, north\nof 32nd Street.\n \n5. 12.\nResolution - Right-of-Way: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute a Memorandum of\nAgreement, and related documents, by and between the City of Lubbock and Lalo E. Gonzales and\nMaria J. Gonzales, for the purchase of a 0.2295-acre parcel located in Section 42, Block AK, Lubbock\nCounty, Texas (Parcel 78), located on the west side of Upland Avenue, south of 19th Street, and north\nof 21st Street, to be utilized for the 2022 Street Bond Project. \n \n5. 13.\nResolution - Right-of-Way: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute an Aerial Street\nUse License Agreement for installation of aerial awning, and a Surface Street Use License for\ninstallation of new Brick Veneer, located Northeast of Lot 20, Block 86, of the Original Town of\nLubbock in Section 1, Block O, at the intersection of 9th Street and Avenue J, by and between the City\nof Lubbock and Jackson Retirement Investments, for a portion of a dedicated street and an awning. \n\n5. 14.\nResolution - Engineering: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute Change Order No. 1\nto Public Works Contract 19060, by and between the City of Lubbock and Lone Star Dirt & Paving,\nLTD., for Milwaukee Avenue Reconstruction from 4th Street to Marshall Street, to be utilized for the\n2022 Street Bond Project.\n \n5. 15.\nResolution - Water Utilities: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute Service Contract\n19328, with Odessa Pumps and Equipment, LLC., to provide large pump repair services for the Water\nand Wastewater Division. \n \n5. 16.\nResolution: Public Health Services: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute an\nInterlocal Agreement, and all related documents, by and between the City of Lubbock and Lubbock\nCounty Hospital District dba University Medical Center, for Clinical Laboratory Services.\n \n5. 17.\nResolution: Public Health Services: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute an\nagreement, and all related documents, by and between the City of Lubbock and Lubbock County\nHospital District dba University Medical Center, for Community Connect Electronic Health Records.\n \n5. 18.\nResolution - Environmental Health: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute\nInterlocal Cooperation Contract No. HHS001719600031, and all related documents, by and between\nthe City of Lubbock and the State of Texas, acting by and through the Department of State Health\nServices, for Mobile Food Inspection Services.\n \n5. 19.\nResolution - Lubbock Police Department: Consider a resolution authorizing the Mayor to execute an\nInterlocal Agreement, by and between the City of Lubbock and Lubbock County, for creating the\nLubbock Crimes Against Children Unit. \n \n5. 20.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Planning (District 2): Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0058, for Zone Case\n1154-D, a request of Jeremy Davis, for a zone change from Neighborhood Commercial District (NC)\nto Auto-Urban Commercial District (AC), at 2518 Parkway Drive, located south of Parkway Drive and\nwest of Zenith Avenue, Oates Addition, Lot 3. \n \n5. 21.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Planning (District 4): Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0059, for Zone Case\n3543, a request for zone changes in City Council District 4 from Low Density Single-Family District\n(SF-2), Medium Density Residential District (MDR), High Density Residential District (HDR), Office\nDistrict (OF), Neighborhood Commercial District (NC), and Heavy Commercial District (HC), to Low\nDensity Single-Family District (SF-2), Medium Density Residential District (MDR), High Density\nResidential District (HDR), Office District (OF), Neighborhood Commercial District (NC),\nAuto-Urban Commercial District (AC), and Heavy Commercial District (HC), at 3201 and 3223 South\nLoop 289, Tracts C and H, Live Oak Addition, 7414 Elgin Avenue, 6.47 acres out of Tract N, Melonie\nGardens Addition, 2516, 2514, 2512, and 2510 81st Street, Lots 52 and 54-56, Gatewood Addition,\n2803 114th Street, 11.81 acres of unplatted land out of Block E-2, Section 21, 3001 114th Street, 6.49\nacres of unplatted land out of Block E-2, Section 21, 3101 114th Street, 25.88 acres of unplatted land\nout of Block E-2, Section 21, 3102 116th Street, 1.91 acres of unplatted land out of Block E-2, Section\n21, 12601 Indiana Avenue, 11.10 acres of unplatted land out of Block E-2, Section 21, 12605 Indiana\nAvenue, Tract A, Discount Shops on Indiana Addition, 12701 Indiana Avenue, 6.7 acres of unplatted\nland out of Block E-2, Section 21, 12709 Indiana Avenue, Tract A, Worship Center 1 Addition, 3802\n130th Street, 3.64 acres of unplatted land out of Block E-2, Section 22, 3814 130th Street, Tract A, less\nthe right-of-way, First Presbyterian Church Addition, 3815 130th Street, 1.22 acres out of Tract F-1,\nKelsey Park Addition, 13005 Norfolk Avenue, 1.23 acres of unplatted land out of Block AK, Section 4,\n3714 146th Street, 0.75 acres of unplatted land out of Block AK, Section 4, 14401 – 14412 Kenosha\nDrive, Lots 119 – 130, Eastwick at Kelsey Park Addition, 11209 Slide Road, Tract A less the west 5\n\nfeet of right-of-way, Raney Addition, 11912 Slide Road, 1.02 acres of unplatted land out of Block E-2,\nSection 24, 12108 Slide Road, 0.91 acres of unplatted land out of Block E-2, Section 24, 12116 Slide\nRoad, 1.5 acres of unplatted land out of Block E-2, Section 24, 12302 Slide Road, the east 240 feet of\nthe north half of Tract A less 810.467 square feet of right-of-way, Sandy Mariah Estates Addition,\n12308 Slide Road, the east half of the south half of Tract A less the east 4.89 feet, Sandy Mariah\nEstates Addition, 5103 82nd Street, 0.08 acres out of Tract J, Lakeridge Country Club Estates\nAddition, 5105 82nd Street, Tract I-8, Lakeridge Country Club Estates Addition, 5107 82nd Street,\n2.32 acres out of Tract I-7-A, Lakeridge Country Club Estates Addition, 5109 82nd Street, Tracts I-5\nand I-6-A, Lakeridge Country Club Estates Addition, 5109 82nd Street Rear and 8215 Slide Road,\nTract I-3, Lakeridge Country Club Estates Addition, 5111 82nd Street, Tract I-4, Lakeridge Country\nClub Estates Addition, 8209 Slide Road, Tract I-1, Lakeridge Country Club Estates Addition, and 8211\nSlide Road, Tract I-2, Lakeridge Country Club Estates Addition. \n \n5. 22.\nOrdinance 2nd Reading - Planning (District 6): Consider Ordinance No. 2026-O0060, for Zone Case\n2538-PP, a request of Parkhill for Lewis Farms Commercial, LLC, and Kinsey 2015 Real Estate Trust,\nfor a zone change from Low Density Single-Family District (SF-2) to Auto-Urban Commercial District\n(AC), generally located north of 4th Street and east of Upland Avenue on 33.7 acres of uplatted land\nout of Block JS, Section 3. \n \n6.\nRegular Agenda\n \n6. 1.\nPublic Hearing - Planning (District 2): Consider a request for Zone Case 2565-I, a request of Hugo\nReed & Associates for CRS Business Park, LLC, for a zone change from Heavy Commercial District\n(HC) and Industrial Park District (IP) to Heavy Commercial District (HC), at 101 66th Street, 103 66th\nStreet, 107 66th Street, 6660 Ash Avenue, 6662 Ash Avenue, 7002 Ash Avenue, 7008 Ash Avenue,\nand 7010 Ash Avenue. Generally located south of 66th Street and west of Ash Avenue, Crossroads\nSouth Business Park Add