 p.m. Citizens Tower, 2nd Floor Conference Center Rooms 201A & 201B 1314 Avenue K Lubbock, TX 79401 (1) Call to Order (2) Citizen Comments - According to HB 2840, any citizen wishing to appear before a regular meeting of Veterans Advisory Committee, regarding any matter posted on the Veterans Advisory Committee Agenda, shal", "text": "Veterans Advisory Committee \nAgenda \nApril 23rd, 2026 \n12:00 p.m. \n \nCitizens Tower, 2nd Floor Conference Center \nRooms 201A & 201B \n1314 Avenue K \nLubbock, TX 79401 \n\n(1) \nCall to Order \n \n(2) \nCitizen Comments - According to HB 2840, any citizen wishing to appear before a regular \nmeeting of Veterans Advisory Committee, regarding any matter posted on the Veterans \nAdvisory Committee Agenda, shall complete the sign-up form provided at the meeting, no \nlater than 12:00 p.m. \n \n(3) \nMinutes: Consider and act on the approval of the minutes from the March 26, 2026 \nVeterans Advisory Committee meeting. \n \n(4) \nRestructuring of Committees & Sub-Committees \n \n(5) \nDiscuss West Texas Salute to Veterans and take appropriate action as needed \n \n(6) \nUpdate on the West Texas State Veterans Cemetery \n \n(7) \nUpdate from the Veterans Advisory Committee Mission and Vision Sub-Committee and \ntake appropriate action as needed \n \n(8) \nUpdate from the Purple Heart Coin Sub-Committee and take appropriate action as needed \n \n(9) \nPresentation from Veteran Housing Sub-Committee (3-5 minutes) \n \n(10) Presentation from Veteran Mental Health Sub-Committee (3-5 minutes) \n \n(11) Presentation from Veteran’s Court Sub-Committee (3-5 minutes) \n \n(12) Presentation from Women Veterans Sub-Committee (3-5 minutes) \n \n(13) Adjourn \n \nDate of next scheduled meeting: May 28th, 2026"}, {"title": "2026-04-22 - Model Codes and Construction Advisory Board (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_04222026-37", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "Current Board Members Gary Ferguson, Chair James Jordan, Vice Chair Kendall Wood, Master Electrician Ryan Farquhar, Commercial Contractor David Small, Engineer Logan West, Facilities Manager Craig Ray, WTHBA Brian Robertson, Engineer Wendell Burris, Lubbock Apartment Marvin White, Licensed HVAC George Henson, Licensed Plumber Jacob Cline, Electrician Model Codes and Construction Advi", "text": "Current Board Members \n\nGary Ferguson, Chair \nJames Jordan, Vice Chair \nKendall Wood, Master Electrician \nRyan Farquhar, Commercial Contractor \nDavid Small, Engineer \nLogan West, Facilities Manager \nCraig Ray, WTHBA \nBrian Robertson, Engineer \nWendell Burris, Lubbock Apartment \nMarvin White, Licensed HVAC \nGeorge Henson, Licensed Plumber \nJacob Cline, Electrician \nModel Codes and Construction Advisory - Meeting Agenda \nApril 22, 2026, 3:30 P.M. \nCitizens Tower \n2nd Floor, Room 201A/B \n1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas \nModel Codes and Construction Advisory Board meetings are available to all \npeople regardless of disability. If you require special assistance, please contact \nthe Building Safety Department at 806.775.3191, e-mail \nmvillagrana@mylubbock.us, or write to Post Office Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas \n79457 at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting. \n \nCall to Order for Regular Meeting \n1. \nApproval of Minutes \na. \nJanuary 28,2026 Regular meeting \nb. \nMarch 25,2026 Regular Meeting \nAction Items \n2. \nThe Board will discuss and take appropriate action on the following items: \nDates at the end of each code set are proposed for presentations (may fluctuate) \na. \n2021/2024 International Swimming Pool and Spa Code - April 2026 \nb. \n2021/2024 International Existing Building Code – Completed -July 2025 \nc. \n2021/2024 International Fuel Gas Code – Completed-March 2026 \nd. \n2021/2024 International Plumbing Code- May 2026 \ne. \n2021/2024 International Mechanical Code – May 2026 \nf. \n2020/2023/2026 National Electric Code – July 2026 \ng. \n2021/2024 International Building Code-Completed- January 2026 \nh. \n2021/2024 International Energy Conservation Code –May 2026 \n\ni. \n2021/2024 International Fire Code – Partial Completion -January 2026 \nj. \n2021/2024 International Residential Code- June 2026"}, {"title": "2026-04-22 - Keep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee Meeting - 12:00pm (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_04222026-31", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "4/13/2026S:\\solid_waste\\Keep Lubbock Beautiful\\Advisory Committee\\0 Meeting Files 0\\Agenda\\2026\\Apr222026.doc Keep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee Agenda April 22, 2026 12:00 p.m. 208 Municipal Dr. 1) Call to Order 2) Citizen Comment – Notice: Any citizen wishing to appear before any regular meeting of the Keep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee shall advise Keep Lubbock Beautifu", "text": "4/13/2026S:\\solid_waste\\Keep Lubbock Beautiful\\Advisory Committee\\0 Meeting Files 0\\Agenda\\2026\\Apr222026.doc \n \nKeep Lubbock Beautiful \nAdvisory Committee Agenda \nApril 22, 2026 12:00 p.m. \n208 Municipal Dr. \n\n1) Call to Order \n\n2) Citizen Comment – Notice: Any citizen wishing to appear before any regular meeting of the Keep Lubbock \nBeautiful Advisory Committee shall advise Keep Lubbock Beautiful of that fact no later than seven calendar \ndays before the meeting at which the citizen wishes to appear. Any citizen wishing to appear shall inform Keep \nLubbock Beautiful, in writing, of the subject of the appearance in sufficient detail. Such notice shall contain the \nname and address of the requestor. The appearance of any citizen giving such notice to Keep Lubbock Beautiful \nshall take precedence in addressing the Keep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee during the Citizen \nComments period. Any citizen failing to advise Keep Lubbock Beautiful of his/her wish to appear before the \nKeep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee as herein above set forth shall, time permitting, be permitted to \naddress the Keep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee after those having given notice. In accordance with \nthe Texas Open Meetings Act, the Keep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee may not take action on public \nmatters during Citizen Comments. \n \n3) Approval of Minutes – March 11, 2026 meeting \n \n4) Work Session \n \na. Annual Art Contest \nb. Beautification Projects \nc. Trainings Review \nd. Community Outreach \ne. Programs Review \nf. Review calendar of events \n\nThe above referenced NOTICE OF MEETING posted on the bulletin board outside the east entrance of \nCitizens Tower, 1314 Ave K, Lubbock, Texas, on the _____day of April 2026 at ________ A.M. /P.M. \n\nBy: ____________________________________________________ \n\nKeep Lubbock Beautiful Advisory Committee meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. \nIf you require special assistance, please contact the City of Lubbock at 806-775-3149 or write to P.O. Box \n2000, Lubbock, Texas, 79457, at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting."}, {"title": "2026-04-20 - Library Board-12:00pm, April 20, 2026 (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_04202026-29", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "City of Lubbock, Texas Library Board Meeting April 20th, at 12:00 PM Mahon Community Room 1306 9th St, Lubbock, TX 79407 1) Call to Order Welcome and introductions – Sheri Lewis 2) Minutes Consider the approval of the March 16th, 2026 meeting minutes. 3) Citizen Comments According to City of Lubbock Board Rules, any citizen wishing to appear before a regular meeting of the Library", "text": "City of Lubbock, Texas \nLibrary Board Meeting \nApril 20th, at 12:00 PM \nMahon Community Room \n1306 9th St, Lubbock, TX 79407 \n \n1) Call to Order \nWelcome and introductions – Sheri Lewis \n \n2) Minutes \nConsider the approval of the March 16th, 2026 meeting minutes. \n \n3) Citizen Comments \nAccording to City of Lubbock Board Rules, any citizen wishing to appear before a regular meeting of the \nLibrary Board, regarding any matter posted on the Library Board Agenda below, shall complete the sign-up \nform provided at the meeting, no later than 12:00 p.m. Any citizen wishing to comment on any matter posted on \nthe Library Board agenda below that will not be in attendance in person may submit a citizen comment by email \nat HStewart@mylubbock.us, no later than 8:00 a.m. on the date of the meeting. Submitted comments must \ninclude name and address. Each comment will be read aloud for a period of time not to exceed three minutes \npursuant to City of Lubbock Board Rules. Citizen Comments is an opportunity for citizens to make comments \nand express a position on agenda items. Any comment received that is in the nature of asking a question will be \nreferred to an appropriate member of the library or City staff for a response and will not be read aloud at the \nmeeting. In accordance with the Texas Open Meetings Act, the Libraries Board may not take action on public \nmatters during Citizen Comments. \n \n4) Presentations \n 4.1) Meet the Staff \n 4.2) Lubbock Library Director Report – Hannah Stewart, Lubbock Library Director \n 4.3) FOL President Report – Tim Ebelthite, FOL President \n 4.4) Genealogical Society Report- Kathy Kitten \n\n5) Work Session \n 5.1) Discussion – A discussion pertaining to housekeeping items and future meeting agenda items. \n \n 5.2) Next regularly scheduled meeting will be at noon on May 18th, 2026 at the Mahon Library. \n\nLubbock Libraries Board meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special assistance, please contact the City of \nLubbock at 806-775-2826 or write to 1306 9th Street, Lubbock, TX 79401 at least 48 hours in advance of the meeting."}, {"title": "2026-03-05 - Planning and Zoning Commission (Agenda)", "url": "https://www.mylubbock.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_03052026-4", "category": "Agenda", "source": "ExposeTexas", "summary": "Planning and Zoning Commission Agenda March 5, 2026 Regular Meeting 6:00 P.M. Citizens Tower Council Chambers 1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas ___________________________________________________________________________________ The Planning and Zoning Commission meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you require special assistance, please contact the City of Lubb", "text": "Planning and Zoning Commission Agenda \nMarch 5, 2026 \nRegular Meeting 6:00 P.M. \n \nCitizens Tower Council Chambers \n1314 Avenue K, Lubbock, Texas \n___________________________________________________________________________________ \n \nThe Planning and Zoning Commission meetings are available to all persons regardless of disability. If you \nrequire special assistance, please contact the City of Lubbock at 806-775-2108, email \ncityplanning@mylubbock.us, or write to P.O. Box 2000, Lubbock, Texas, 79457, at least 48 hours in \nadvance of the meeting. \n \nThe Planning and Zoning Commission of the City of Lubbock, Texas reserves the right to meet in closed \nsession on any of the items listed below should the need arise and if applicable pursuant to authorization by \nSection 551.071 of the Texas Government Code. \n \nRegular Agenda \n \n1. Call to Order \n \n1.1 Citizen Comments – According to Lubbock Planning and Zoning Commission Rules, any \ncitizen wishing to appear before a regular meeting of the Planning and Zoning Commission, \nregarding any matter posted on the Planning and Zoning Commission Agenda below, shall \ncomplete the sign-up form provided at the meeting, no later than 6:00 p.m. \n \n2. Approval of Minutes \n \n2.1 February 5, 2026 Regular Planning and Zoning Commission Meeting minutes. \n \n3. Zone Changes - Public Hearings \nPlanning & Zoning Commission makes recommendation; City Council has final authority for approval. \n \nDistrict 2 \n3.1 Zone Case 774-D: UN2 Corporation, request for a zone change from Light Industrial \nDistrict (LI) to Heavy Commercial District (HC), at: \n• 1129 Southeast Loop 289, located north of Southeast Loop 289 and southwest of East \nSlaton Road, Plan-Ex No.1 Addition, Lot 6. \n \nDistrict 4 \n \nDrew Gray \nTerri Morris \nStacey Rogers \nRobert Wood \nJames Bell, Chair \nTarek Redwan, Vice-Chair \nRenee Cage \nKirk Franklin \nScott Gloyna \n\n3.2 Zone Case 3553: Parkhill for Baxter Trusts, request for a zone change from Low Density \nSingle-Family District (SF-2), Medium Density Residential District (MDR), Neighborhood \nCommercial District (NC), and Auto-Urban Commercial District (AC) to Low Density Single-\nFamily District (SF-2) and Auto-Urban Commercial District (AC), at: \n• \nGenerally located west of Indiana Avenue and south of 114th Street, on 20.26 acres of \nunplatted land out of Block E-2, Section 22. \nDistrict 5 \n3.3 Zone Case 3016-G: R2M Engineering, LLC, for Enrico G. & Teresita A. Aguas, request for \na zone change from Office District (OF) to Neighborhood Commercial District (NC), at: \n• \n9901 Upland Avenue, located east of Upland Avenue and south of 98th Street, on \n1.615 acres of unplatted land out of Block AK, Section 22. \nDistrict 3 \n3.4 Zone Case 3542: A request for zone changes in City Council District 3 from Low Density \nSingle-Family District (SF-2), High Density Residential District (HDR), Neighborhood \nCommercial District (NC), and Heavy Commercial (HC) to Office District (OF) and Auto-\nUrban Commercial District (AC), at: \n• \n4321 Marsha Sharp Freeway, Lots 1-2, Dyer Addition and Lot 4, Block 4, less the \nright-of-way, Jarrott Addition, 4302 22nd Place, Lot 3, Block 4, John W Jarrott \nAddition, 4301 Marsha Sharp Freeway, Lots 1, 2, and 5, Block 4, John W Jarrott \nAddition, 4110 22nd Place, Lots 1-2, Block 6, John W Jarrott Addition, 4120 22nd \nPlace, Lot 4, Block 6, John W Jarrott Addition, 4122 22nd Place, Lot 3, Block 6, John \nW Jarrott Addition, 4119 Marsha Sharp Freeway, Lot 3, Cope Addition, 4115 \nMarsha Sharp Freeway, Lot 2-A, Cope Addition, 4105 Marsha Sharp Freeway, \nLots 1-B-1 and 1-C, less the right-of-way, Cope Addition, 4105 19th Street, Lot 5, less \nthe right-of-way, Ashley Addition, 4009 19th Street, Lots 1-A and 2, less the right-of-\nway, Ted Quan Addition, 4001 19th Street, north part of Lot 3, Charles Addition, 1914 \nNashville Avenue, the south 171.6 feet of Lot 3, Charles Addition, 2006 Nashville \nAvenue, Lot 1-B, Ted Quan Addition, 3901 19th Street, Tract A, J O Smith Addition, \n3723 19th Street, Lot 6, less 381 square feet and the northwest part of Lot 5 and 645 \nsquare feet of closed 19th Street, Block 1, Murphy Place Addition, 3703 19th Street, \nLots 1-4 and Lot 5, less the northwest part, Block 1, Murphy Place Addition, 3704 20th \nStreet, Lots 7-14, Block 1, Murphy Place Addition, 3802 and 3804 21st Street, Lots \n5-8, Units 1-5, Building B, Block 2, Reeder Addition, 3801, 3809, and 3815 21st \nStreet, Lots 1-8, Block 1, Jim Floyd Addition, 4001 and 4003 21st Street, Lots 1-2 \nand 759.375 square foot strip out of Block B, Section 15, Block 1, Agnew-Kendrick \nAddition, 3802 22nd Street, Lots 10-14, Block 1, Jim Floyd Addition, 4002 22nd \nStreet, Lot 17, Block 1, Agnew-Kendrick Addition, 2107 Oxford Avenue and 4010 \n22nd Street, Lots 9-16, Block 1, Agnew-Kendrick Addition, 2201 Oxford Avenue, \nTracts B-1 and C, Williams Addition, 4002 and 4014 22nd Place, Tracts B-2 and A, \nWilliams Addition, 3821 22nd Street, Lots 2-5 and the west 10.75 feet of Lot 1, Block \n1, J H Webb Addition, 3801, 3805, and 3809 22nd Street, the east 47 feet of Lot 1, \nBlock 1, J H Webb Addition and Lots 1-6, Block 1, J R Brock Addition, 4417 50th \n\nStreet, Lots 1-B and 1-C, Block 1, Sylvan Dell Heights Addition, and 4501 50th Street, \nLot 8-A, Block 8, Sylvan Dell Heights Addition. \n• \n4. Adjourn \n\nThe above-referenced NOTICE OF MEETING was posted on the south entrance of Citizens Tower, 1314 \nAvenue K, Lubbock, Texas, on the_________ day of February at _________AM./P.M. \n\nBy: _____________________________________________"}]}